    "location": "Mumbai-New Delhi coordinated protests; Delhi leg at Jantar Mantar and India Gate",
    "cause": "Demonstrators are demanding the immediate resignation of the Chief Election Commissioner over alleged manipulation of electoral rolls and institutional capture of the Election Commission of India.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "Indian authorities have launched a sweeping crackdown on this movement, with thousands detained nationwide and activists and journalists criminalized under multiple FIRs. Law enforcement has used metallic pellet guns against protesters, causing serious injuries, and the CIVICUS Monitor still rates India's civic space as 'repressed.' The coordinated Mumbai-New Delhi nature of the protest and the explicit demand for a constitutional authority's resignation make mass arrests and violent dispersal highly likely.",
    "status": "The Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) and allied groups launched coordinated protests in Mumbai and New Delhi demanding the resignation of the Election Commission chief, with the Delhi leg centered at Jantar Mantar and spilling toward India Gate. Authorities responded with a nationwide clampdown, detaining thousands of demonstrators and filing FIRs against organizers, activists, and journalists covering the events. Metallic pellet guns were used at the 'Cockroach Party' protest, resulting in documented injuries that rights groups have flagged as a brazen violation of human rights in submissions to UN Special Rapporteurs. Despite the crackdown, organizers say they will continue with a nationwide strike and a planned march toward Parliament. The situation remains fluid, with police maintaining a heavy presence and restricting movement around central Delhi.",
