    "status": "The Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) continued its coordinated Mumbai-New Delhi protest demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, with actions resuming on Saturday, October 10, 2026, despite mass detentions of its leaders and supporters. Protests were scattered across multiple locations in Delhi rather than concentrated at a single site, as Delhi Police denied permission for the planned gathering at Jantar Mantar. Authorities implemented sweeping restrictions, including cutting train and metro services, shutting down internet access, and deploying over 35,000 police and paramilitary personnel across the capital, effectively turning Delhi into a fortress. Union Home Secretary Govind Mohan directed police chiefs of all states and Union Territories to coordinate with Delhi Police amid CJP mobilisation concerns. CJP leaders Abhijeet Dipke, Saurav Das, and Ashutosh Ranka remain in custody, though they addressed the India Today Mumbai Conclave 2026 on Friday. A network of over 130 volunteers is coordinating transport for released detainees, medical care, mental health support, and legal assistance. The Supreme Court held a special hearing on October 11 on petitions challenging restrictions on public transport and protest detentions. Organizers have vowed not to back down and plan to continue protests, with INDIA bloc MPs also staging a larger protest against the CEC.",
