    "status": "Thousands of opposition demonstrators, led by Rahul Gandhi and other opposition leaders, marched through central New Delhi on Monday, October 12, 2026, shifting their 'Save Democracy' agitation from the Election Commission to the Supreme Court. The march followed a weekend crackdown in which Delhi police detained more than 2,000 protesters on October 10, including the founder of the 'Cockroach' youth movement, and locked down the capital to prevent the planned protest at the Election Commission. On Monday, police again obstructed the protests, with barricades placed around the Supreme Court as thousands returned to the streets. The opposition petitioned the Supreme Court seeking suspension of voter list changes that removed over 130 million names, and demanded the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. On Tuesday, October 13, top leaders of the 'Cockroach' youth movement were detained after they jumped barricades. Thousands of police officers and security personnel were deployed across central New Delhi for a third straight day. Rahul Gandhi compared the protests to 'tandav' and 'Shivji ki baraat', saying everyone is welcome. The opposition has vowed to continue the agitation despite mass detentions and police obstruction.",
