    "name": "Mumbai Protest Demanding Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's Resignation",
    "location": "August Kranti Maidan, Gowalia Tank, South Mumbai",
    "cause": "Protesters are demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over alleged manipulation of voter rolls that they claim will exclude millions of eligible voters. The movement, led by youth activists and the Gen Z Cockroach Janta Party (CJP), alleges the Election Commission's voter roll revision exercise is designed to disenfranchise opposition-leaning voters ahead of upcoming elections.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level has been raised to critical due to the mass detention of over 7,500 protesters in Delhi over the weekend of October 10-11, 2026, and the detention of top CJP leaders on Tuesday, October 13, 2026, after they jumped barricades. In Mumbai, police have detained thousands of protesters, as confirmed by AP reports and news photographs showing demonstrators being taken into police vehicles at August Kranti Maidan. The nationwide crackdown includes a lockdown and internet blackouts in Delhi, with reports of house arrests and police checks on train journeys, indicating a severe government response. Additionally, saffron-clad groups carrying sticks were seen threatening protesters in central Delhi for a second consecutive day on Sunday, October 11, 2026, raising the risk of communal clashes. While no mass violence or injuries have been confirmed in Mumbai specifically, the scale of detentions, the use of barricades, and the government's refusal to back down create a tense standoff with potential for further escalation.",
    "status": "The Mumbai protest demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, centered at August Kranti Maidan in Gowalia Tank, South Mumbai, remains part of an active nationwide mobilisation led by the Gen Z Cockroach Janta Party (CJP). Mumbai Police have detained protesters at the site, with news photographs showing demonstrators being taken into police vehicles during the CJP protest in Mumbai. The most recent escalation occurred on Tuesday, October 13, 2026, when top leaders of the 'cockroach' youth movement were detained after they jumped barricades, according to Reuters. Over the weekend of October 10-11, 2026, more than 7,500 protesters were detained in Delhi during a massive security crackdown, and Indian authorities also detained thousands of 'Cockroach' movement protesters in Mumbai, as reported by AP. The protests were triggered after authorities removed more than 130 million voters from the electoral list since last year. CJP leaders were released from detention and have pledged to hold more protests, while the Election Commission denies allegations of voter-roll manipulation. The Supreme Court has heard petitions against the CEC and issued notices to the Modi government and the election body, with opposition parties marching to the top court on Monday. No specific next date for Mumbai has been confirmed in the search results, though further protests are pledged.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Mumbai Police have detained protesters at August Kranti Maidan, with news photographs showing demonstrators being taken into police vehicles. Barricades were used, and top CJP leaders were detained after jumping barricades on October 13, 2026. Exact numbers deployed in Mumbai are not specified in the search results.", "Recent incidents: On October 13, 2026, top leaders of the 'Cockroach' youth movement were detained in Mumbai after they jumped barricades, according to Reuters. Over the weekend of October 10-11, 2026, more than 7,500 protesters were detained in Delhi, and thousands were also detained in Mumbai, as reported by AP. No injuries have been confirmed in Mumbai specifically.", "Medical access: No specific information on medical access, hospitals nearby, or ambulances on site is available in the search results. This remains a gap in the intelligence.", "Legal support: The Supreme Court has heard petitions against the CEC and issued notices to the Modi government and the election body. Opposition parties marched to the top court on Monday. CJP leaders were released from detention and have pledged to hold more protests. No specific legal helplines or organizations are mentioned in the search results."],
