    "status": "The Cockroach Janta Party has formally called for nationwide protests on July 24, 2026, with Mumbai expected to be a primary flashpoint alongside New Delhi. Organizers are demanding the resignation of Election Commission chief Gyanesh Kumar and opposing voter roll changes they say threaten voting rights for millions. Thousands are expected to gather at multiple locations including Shivaji Park and central Mumbai, with heavy police deployment anticipated. The July 24 mobilization follows the July 20 protests that saw around 300 detentions and the July 21 Shivaji Park backlash gathering. Authorities are expected to invoke prohibitory orders and deploy large numbers of personnel across the city.",
    "details": ["Anticipated heavy police deployment across Mumbai with barricades, drones, and possible water cannons; Section 144-style prohibitory orders likely in central Mumbai.", "Prior wave on July 20, 2026, saw around 300 detentions; July 21 Shivaji Park gathering followed peacefully; July 24 expected to be larger and riskier.", "Major hospitals on standby include KEM, Sion, and Hinduja; ambulances expected at major gathering points; injury risk elevated given crowd size.", "Civil liberties organizations and legal aid networks preparing for mass detention response; helplines being circulated by organizers; bail teams on standby."],
