    "status": "The Cockroach Movement's voter roll protests remain active in Mumbai, with demonstrations at Dadar, Bandra, Andheri, and Kurla railway station areas. More than 400 protesters, including Bollywood actor Imran Khan, were detained by Mumbai Police during these gatherings. The movement has drawn support from political figures Uddhav and Raj Thackeray, who united for a major protest in Mumbai against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. CJP leaders claim imminent arrest under the National Security Act (NSA) ahead of a planned major gathering at Jantar Mantar in Delhi on October 10. Organizers have refused to seek permits, and crowds continue to swell despite preventive detentions. The situation remains tense as police have threatened arrest under Section 144. The protests are linked to the ECI's re-scrutinisation of nearly 80 million voters, which demonstrators say will deny voting rights to millions.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Mumbai Police detained over 400 protesters at Dadar, Bandra, Andheri, and Kurla railway station areas. Section 144 imposed, with threats of NSA arrests for CJP leaders. Exact numbers of deployed personnel not specified.", "Recent incidents: On October 13, protests continued with mass detentions, including actor Imran Khan. CJP leaders claim imminent NSA arrest ahead of October 10 Delhi gathering. A policeman was suspended for firing an AK-47 at student protesters in another region.", "Medical access: No specific reports of injuries or medical access issues in Mumbai protests. However, the suspension of a policeman for firing an AK-47 at student protesters in another region indicates potential for violence.", "Legal support: CJP leaders face cases over Mumbai demonstration and claim imminent NSA arrest. Legal status of detained protesters unclear. No specific legal helplines or organizations mentioned."],
