    "dangerReason": "Mumbai Police detained multiple student protesters, and the viral video confirms police intimidation tactics, with driver Pawan Sangle threatening to plant '50 grams of powder' on students. Although Sangle was suspended and an inquiry ordered, no criminal case has been filed against him, fueling protester anger and keeping tensions elevated. The protest has expanded into a broader student movement, with CJP founder Abhijeet Dipke announcing a massive mobilisation in Delhi on October 10, increasing the potential for mass mobilization and further police confrontation. No recent physical violence or injuries are reported in the search results, but the threat of poisoning and police crackdown remain central grievances. The lack of fresh on-ground reporting from the Kalina Campus site means the situation could escalate without warning.",
