    "dangerReason": "Around 300 detentions were reported on July 20, 2026, during voter roll protests, and demonstrators regrouped at Shivaji Park on July 21, 2026, despite heavy police deployment. The concentration of detained activists, ongoing police crackdown posture, and the symbolic nature of Shivaji Park as a historic protest ground raise the risk of fresh clashes, re-arrests, and crowd-control escalation. Authorities have already shown willingness to detain en masse, and any attempt to re-detain returnees could trigger confrontations.",
    "status": "Citizens and activists gathered peacefully at Shivaji Park, Dadar West, on July 21, 2026, to protest the roughly 300 detentions carried out the previous day during Cockroach Janta Party voter roll demonstrations. The gathering was framed as a response to what organizers call systemic suppression of peaceful assembly. Mumbai Police maintained a heavy presence around the park with barricades and monitoring, though no fresh detentions were immediately reported at the July 21 gathering. Organizers are demanding the release of those still in custody and have signaled further mobilizations if detentions continue. The protest is directly tied to the broader Cockroach movement's nationwide call for action on July 24.",
    "details": ["Heavy Mumbai Police deployment around Shivaji Park with barricades at all entry points; drones and CCTV monitoring reported; nearby roads partially restricted.", "Approximately 300 detentions reported on July 20, 2026, during voter roll protests; peaceful gathering followed on July 21 at Shivaji Park demanding release of detainees.", "Nearby hospitals include Hinduja Hospital (Mahim) and Sion Hospital; no ambulances confirmed on-site; no injuries reported at the July 21 gathering.", "Legal observers and civil liberties groups monitoring detentions; many detainees released on personal bond; activists seeking legal aid for those still held."],
