    "dangerReason": "The rasta roko completely shut down the Pune-Satara highway (NH-48) at Kapurhol Chowk in Bhor tehsil for hours, stranding thousands of vehicles on a high-speed intercity artery and creating a serious risk of vehicle-pedestrian collisions. Hundreds of farmers and villagers participated, and police were deployed to manage traffic and monitor the blockade, though no forcible clearance or clashes have been reported. The unresolved farmer grievances over the Bhongavli power project, combined with no scheduled talks with state authorities, create a tense standoff with clear potential for escalation. Organizers have explicitly threatened repeat highway blockades and intensified agitation, raising the likelihood of further disruption and possible confrontation with police if clearance is attempted. No injuries, detentions, or violence are confirmed in current reports, which keeps the level at high rather than critical.",
    "status": "Hundreds of farmers and residents from Bhor and Velhe (Rajgad) talukas staged a rasta roko at Kapurhol Chowk in Bhor tehsil, blocking the Pune-Satara highway (NH-48) for several hours and bringing traffic to a standstill. The protest targets the proposed Bhongavli power project and high-tension transmission lines routed through agricultural land in the Bhor-Rajgad belt. Protesters are demanding the project be shifted away from farmland and residential areas and are calling for direct talks with state authorities before any further construction proceeds. Police were deployed to manage traffic and monitor the blockade, with traffic diverted around the affected stretch; no breakthrough or government commitment to talks has been reported. Organizers have indicated they will intensify agitation, including repeat highway blockades, if the state does not commit to negotiations and a project review. No injuries, arrests, or violent clashes have been reported in the available coverage.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Police were deployed at Kapurhol Chowk in Bhor tehsil to manage traffic and monitor the rasta roko on NH-48; traffic was diverted around the blocked stretch. No reports of barricades, water cannons, drones, or forcible clearance measures.", "Recent incidents: Hundreds of farmers and residents from Bhor and Velhe (Rajgad) talukas blocked the Pune-Satara highway for several hours, bringing traffic to a standstill. No injuries, arrests, property damage, or violent clashes have been reported in available coverage.", "Medical access: No injuries or medical emergencies have been reported in connection with the blockade. No information available on ambulances on site or hospital access disruptions; the highway blockade itself may delay emergency vehicles on the affected stretch.", "Legal support: No information available on legal organizations, lawyers, or helplines involved. No reports of detentions or court interventions related to this protest."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-10T04:12:03+00:00","level":"high","status":"Hundreds of farmers and villagers from the Bhor-Rajgad belt staged a rasta roko on the Pune-Satara highway, bringing traffic to a standstill for several hours. The protesters, organized under local fa"},{"date":"2026-10-11T00:09:47+00:00","level":"high","status":"Hundreds of farmers and villagers from the Bhor-Rajgad belt staged a rasta roko on the Pune-Satara highway, bringing traffic to a standstill for several hours. The protesters, organized under local fa"}]
