    "cause": "Hindu Jagran Manch (HJM) supporters marched to SRFTI alleging objectionable content and demanding action against students, while SRFTI students and progressive groups resisted the march, leading to violent clashes between the two sides outside the campus.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "Violence has recurred at SRFTI within a week, with right-wing protesters hurling stones, bricks and bottles at students and clashing with police while attempting to breach the campus gates on October 6, 2026. Two students were injured and classes were suspended, confirming physical harm inside an educational institution. The protesters have made explicit threats against the campus community, and the group has now targeted the institute twice, showing intent and capacity for repeat attacks. Police intervention separated the groups but failed to prevent injuries, and the underlying dispute remains unresolved with FIRs filed but no de-escalation reported. The combination of confirmed injuries, projectiles, repeated mobilisation and an unresolved standoff justifies a critical danger level.",
    "status": "The Satyajit Ray Film and Television Institute (SRFTI) in Panchasayar, Kolkata, remains tense after a second round of violence on October 6, 2026, when supporters of the Bangiya Hindu Jagaran Manch (also reported as Hindu Jagran Manch) marched to the campus and clashed with police while attempting to breach the gates, allegedly hurling stones, bricks and bottles at students. Two students were injured and classes have been suspended. This followed an earlier clash in late September/early October, and the Hindutva group had publicly threatened that 'Dimagi Naxals at the SRFTI will be taught a lesson.' Students had previously written to the I&B Ministry and asked Kolkata Police not to grant permission for the rally. Twin FIRs have been registered after the clashes. Students are now demanding police protection and action against the attackers, and they continue to resist, with the institute on edge. As of October 10, 2026, classes have been suspended for the 11th consecutive day as students continue their class boycott, demanding better campus security.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Kolkata Police were deployed outside SRFTI on October 6, 2026, to prevent protesters from entering the campus; they clashed with the advancing group but no specific numbers, equipment, or road closures were reported.", "Recent incidents: On October 6, 2026, Bangiya Hindu Jagaran Manch supporters tried to breach SRFTI gates, hurled stones, bricks and bottles at students, injuring two; police intervened and twin FIRs were registered. An earlier clash occurred in late September/early October.", "Medical access: Two students were injured in the October 6 clash; no details on hospitals, ambulances, or accessibility were provided in the search results.", "Legal support: Twin FIRs have been registered after the clashes; students have written to the I&B Ministry and the SRFTI chairman, and are demanding police protection and action against attackers, but no specific legal aid organisations or helplines were mentioned."],
