    "status": "The 'Nabanna Abhijan' protest march toward the West Bengal State Secretariat in Howrah remains a live and volatile situation, with the most recent confirmed escalation occurring on August 27, 2026. According to multiple news reports, Kolkata police used tear gas, water cannons, and lathicharge to disperse protesters attempting to march to Nabanna after crowds broke barricades. The BJP called for a 12-hour Bengal Bandh on Wednesday, August 28, in response to the police crackdown, while the ruling TMC denounced the bandh call. Ahead of the march, police had implemented extensive security measures, including a high-security ring around the secretariat, and cast doubts on the organisers, labeling them 'illegal' and 'politically motivated'. The march was organized by an unregistered body claiming to be a students' organisation. The BJP has demanded the release of students arrested during the march. As of the latest reports, no fresh march date has been announced, but the confrontation has raised concerns about further clashes if the agitation continues.",
