    "status": "The Anti-'Cockroach' Movement Solidarity Protest in Kolkata remains active but no new Kolkata-specific gathering has been confirmed since the July 24, 2026 clash at Esplanade, where a CJP-Left students' rally from Sealdah was blocked by police and tear gas was used, leaving several injured. Nationally, the movement continues to expand: the Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) has called for nationwide protests, and over a 48-hour period student-led protests engulfed almost every state despite FIRs, lathi charges and water cannons. On October 11-12, 2026, former CM Mamata Banerjee and TMC MPs were detained for nearly four hours in Delhi, and 'cockroach' movement leaders have publicly vowed to keep up election-related protests. West Bengal's government has invoked the Goonda Act against 14 arrested protesters, including 13 Muslims, while the Chief Minister has used communal rhetoric ('Friday people', 'Jamatis', 'Islamists') to characterize demonstrators. Organizers plan further nationwide actions, but no specific new Kolkata date or venue has been confirmed in the latest reports.",
