    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to recent incidents of self-immolation and clashes with police. A street vendor attempted self-immolation during a BMC encroachment drive at 10 Number Market, indicating extreme desperation. Additionally, traders clashed with police, broke barricades, and disrupted traffic during a protest march from New Market towards CM House. These events, combined with ongoing demolitions and the threat of an indefinite strike, elevate the risk of further escalation and violence. The recent relocation of 35 families from Deepak Nagar slum to Bag Mugalia adds to the tension, as residents protest the move.",
    "status": "Residents and traders in Bhopal continue to hold rival marches over land-use demands as a Supreme Court deadline looms. Traders are demanding a mixed-use policy and a new master plan to protect businesses, while residents are urging action on illegal constructions. The Bhopal Municipal Corporation (BMC) has continued its anti-encroachment drives, including demolishing 63 illegal structures near the Upper Lake and clearing encroachments across the city. A street vendor attempted self-immolation during a BMC drive at 10 Number Market, and traders clashed with police, breaking barricades and disrupting traffic during a march from New Market towards CM House. Additionally, on Saturday, the district administration shifted 35 families from Deepak Nagar slum to Bag Mugalia as part of the anti-encroachment drive, sparking further protests. The agitation remains ongoing with no reports of mass violence or detentions, but tensions are high.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Not specified in search results; however, clashes with police and barricade-breaking during a traders' march from New Market to CM House indicate a significant police deployment in central Bhopal.", "Recent incidents: A street vendor attempted self-immolation during a BMC drive at 10 Number Market; traders clashed with police, broke barricades, and disrupted traffic during a march from New Market towards CM House; 35 families were shifted from Deepak Nagar slum to Bag Mugalia on Saturday.", "Medical access: No information available in search results regarding hospitals, ambulances, or medical access for injured protesters.", "Legal support: No information available in search results regarding legal organizations, lawyers, helplines, or court interventions for detained protesters."],
