    "name": "Telangana Polytechnic Students 'Chalo Hyderabad' March (Aug 22)",
    "location": "Assembly route from Government Polytechnic College campuses across Telangana converging at Hyderabad city centre (Dharna Chowk / Indira Park area)",
    "cause": "Government polytechnic colleges were brought under the ambit of Young India Skill University as part of a state restructuring, and students are marching against the merger, fearing loss of autonomy, diploma recognition and existing fee/syllabus protections.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "This is a large-scale, multi-district mobilisation ('Chalo Hyderabad') explicitly modelled on earlier student marches that drew heavy police deployment and barricading in Hyderabad. Polytechnic students have already staged a prior 'Chalo Hyderabad' march against the same SHAKTI/Young India Skill University merger, indicating a repeat confrontation with police at Dharna Chowk and Indira Park, where Section 144-style restrictions and barricades are routinely imposed. Mass detention of marching students, road closures on major arteries, and possible lathi-charge or water-cannon use at choke points near the Assembly are realistic risks given the state's firm posture against student agitation.",
    "status": "Government polytechnic students across Telangana have announced a fresh 'Chalo Hyderabad' march for August 22, 2026, escalating their campaign against the merger of polytechnic colleges into Young India Skill University. Organisers say contingents from district polytechnic campuses will converge on Hyderabad, with the main body gathering at Dharna Chowk and Indira Park before attempting to march toward the Assembly and Higher Education offices. This follows an earlier Polytechnic 'Chalo Hyderabad' march against the SHAKTI Department merger, which was met with police barricading and detentions. Student unions are coordinating through campus committees and social media, and have appealed for a peaceful, disciplined march. Police have not yet issued formal permission, and Hyderabad and Cyberabad police are expected to deploy large numbers at entry points to the city and around the Assembly. Students plan to submit a memorandum to the Higher Education Minister and threaten an indefinite sit-in if demands are not met.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Heavy deployment expected at Dharna Chowk, Indira Park, Tank Bund, and Assembly approach roads; barricades, RSI (Rapid Action Force) units, drones and possible water cannons; city entry points from NH-44 and NH-65 likely to be picketed.", "Recent incidents: A previous Polytechnic 'Chalo Hyderabad' march against the SHAKTI Department merger saw students stopped at barricades and detained; Nizam College students separately protested over hostel accommodation after rooms were not allotted for over a month.", "Medical access: Osmania General Hospital and Gandhi Hospital are the nearest major government facilities to the Dharna Chowk/Assembly belt; NIMS is accessible from Punjagutta. No dedicated ambulances confirmed on site; organisers have been asked to arrange first-aid volunteers.", "Legal support: Student unions and civil-liberties lawyers associated with the Telangana Vidyarthi Vedika and similar groups are expected to provide legal aid; no dedicated helpline announced yet. Detained students in past marches were released on personal bond after station-level processing."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-11T12:27:36+00:00","level":"high","status":"Government polytechnic students across Telangana have announced a fresh 'Chalo Hyderabad' march for August 22, 2026, escalating their campaign against the merger of polytechnic colleges into Young Ind"}]
