    "name": "Chennai Sanitary Workers' Strike Enters Fourth Day at Ripon Buildings",
    "location": "Ripon Buildings, Greater Chennai Corporation Headquarters, Park Town, Chennai",
    "cause": "Sanitary workers are demanding job regularisation, an increase in daily wage to Rs 832, a weekly paid-off, and maternity leave benefits. The union is also seeking a direct audience with the Chief Minister to address their long-pending grievances.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to the recent flash protest where over 50 sanitation workers stormed the Ripon Building, breaching security and creating tense moments that required police intervention. The strike has entered its fourth day with hundreds of workers participating, and garbage accumulation poses public health risks. Police presence is significant with barricades around Ripon Buildings to prevent marches toward the Secretariat, and previous sanitation strikes in Chennai have led to scuffles and mass detentions. The union's threat to intensify agitation and expand to other zones, combined with the lack of government response, increases the potential for confrontations and arrests. The Madras High Court's past orders to clear protest sites indicate a legal pressure point that could lead to forced dispersal.",
    "status": "The Chennai sanitary workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers continuing their sit-in protest. The workers are demanding job regularisation, a daily wage increase to Rs 832, a weekly paid-off, and maternity leave benefits. Union representatives have sought an audience with the Chief Minister but have not received a positive response. Garbage has begun piling up in several neighbourhoods, raising public health concerns. The union has announced that the strike will continue indefinitely and may expand to other corporation zones if no government response is forthcoming. A recent flash protest saw more than 50 sanitation workers storm the Ripon Building, entering the premises and creating tense moments before police intervened. The Madras High Court has previously intervened in similar strikes, ordering site clearance, but the current strike continues without a court resolution.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Significant police deployment at Ripon Buildings with barricades to prevent marches toward the Secretariat. Exact numbers not specified in available reports.", "Recent incidents: On Tuesday, more than 50 sanitation workers stormed the Ripon Building in a flash protest, entering the premises and creating tense moments before police intervened. No injuries or arrests reported.", "Medical access: No specific information available on medical access or injuries. General public health concerns due to garbage accumulation.", "Legal support: The Madras High Court has previously intervened in similar strikes, ordering site clearance. No current court resolution or legal support details available."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-11T04:18:33+00:00","level":"high","status":"The sanitation workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers from across Greater Chennai Corporation zones continuing their sit-in pr"},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:19:31+00:00","level":"high","status":"The sanitation workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers from across Greater Chennai Corporation zones continuing their sit-in pr"},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:11:56+00:00","level":"high","status":"The Chennai sanitary workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers continuing their sit-in protest. The workers are demanding job reg"},{"date":"2026-10-12T12:15:50+00:00","level":"high","status":"The Chennai sanitary workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers continuing their sit-in protest. The workers are demanding job reg"},{"date":"2026-10-13T12:09:42+00:00","level":"high","status":"The Chennai sanitary workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers continuing their sit-in protest. The workers are demanding job reg"},{"date":"2026-10-14T00:16:49+00:00","level":"high","status":"The Chennai sanitary workers' strike at Ripon Buildings has entered its fourth day as of Sunday, with hundreds of conservancy workers continuing their sit-in protest. The workers are demanding job reg"}]
