    "dangerReason": "The protest has remained largely peaceful, involving a legislative boycott, sit-in, and dharna outside the Assembly, with no reports of physical violence, injuries, or mass detentions. Police blocked Congress MLAs and workers from entering a Jaipur school on August 20, but the situation did not escalate beyond political sloganeering. The introduction of the UCC Bill amid protests indicates escalating political confrontation, but the danger level remains moderate as the agitation is currently non-violent.",
    "status": "Congress MLAs boycotted the first day of the Rajasthan Assembly monsoon session on August 20, staging a dharna outside the Vidhan Sabha in Jyoti Nagar, Jaipur, over alleged restrictions on outsider entry and media access to schools. Leader of Opposition Tikaram Jully and other Congress MLAs were blocked by police from entering a Jaipur school, after which they led a march to the Assembly. The BJP government tabled the Uniform Civil Code (UCC) Bill amid sloganeering by Congress MLAs, and the session was adjourned within 21 minutes. Congress leaders have indicated they will continue their agitation both inside and outside the legislature, and the standoff remains unresolved.",
