    "location": "Jantar Mantar-style protest site, near Gujarat University campus, Navrangpura, Ahmedabad",
    "cause": "Youth-led Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) activists are continuing their hunger strike over voter list irregularities and electoral transparency demands, following a federal minister's promise of talks on July 20. The movement demands a formal review of voter roll deletions and restoration of removed names ahead of upcoming elections.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "Hunger strikers are in a medically precarious state after multiple days without food, with at least 3 participants reportedly hospitalized in Ahmedabad. The protest has drawn counter-mobilization from right-wing groups who have previously attacked CJP-adjacent book reading events in Vastrapur on August 27, injuring 8-10 people. Police have erected barricades around the site but have not ruled out preventive detention of organizers under Section 144 if the strike continues.",
    "status": "Approximately 40-60 CJP activists and student supporters remain gathered at the Navrangpura protest site as of the latest update, with 5 on active hunger strike and 3 hospitalized at Civil Hospital. The federal minister's July 20 promise of talks has not yet materialized into a formal meeting, prompting organizers to vow an indefinite continuation. Ahmedabad Police have deployed 2 platoons of the State Reserve Police with barricades at all approach roads, and have videographed the site for potential FIRs. Organizers plan to escalate with a candlelight march toward Gandhinagar if no ministerial response arrives within 72 hours. NSUI and Gen Z student groups have pledged solidarity turnout.",
