    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to the confirmed August 27, 2026 attack on a silent reading session in Vastrapur, where alleged VHP and Bajrang Dal members assaulted participants, tore books, and caused 8-10 injuries. Three arrests were made, but FIRs against 20 individuals—including students and organizers—have escalated tensions and prompted follow-up protests demanding withdrawal of charges. The involvement of organized right-wing groups with a history of confrontational tactics in the same neighborhood creates a substantial risk of repeat clashes. Police have maintained a visible presence with barricades around Vastrapur Lake and the Anand Niketan area, indicating ongoing security concerns. Both sides continue to mobilize, and the lack of de-escalation or resolution suggests the potential for further violence remains elevated.",
    "status": "The follow-up protest in Vastrapur, Ahmedabad, remains centered on the August 27, 2026 disruption of a silent reading session featuring Malala Yousafzai's 'I Am Malala' and Anne Frank's 'The Diary of a Young Girl' at AUDA Garden. On that evening, alleged VHP and Bajrang Dal members attacked participants, tore books, and clashed with attendees, leaving 8-10 people injured. Police arrested three individuals in connection with the violence, while FIRs were registered against 20 people, including students and organizers, sparking demands for withdrawal of charges. In a related act of solidarity, citizens held a silent reading protest at Law Garden to defend the 'right to read' after the books were removed from a school reading list. Organizers plan further silent reading sessions and continue pressing the state government to drop the FIRs, while VHP and Bajrang Dal have signaled they will keep opposing such events. Police maintain a visible presence around Vastrapur Lake and the Anand Niketan area, with barricades at key entry points, and the situation remains tense as both sides mobilize supporters.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Visible police deployment around Vastrapur Lake and Anand Niketan area, with barricades at key entry points to AUDA Garden; exact numbers not specified in reports.", "Recent incidents: On August 27, 2026, alleged VHP/Bajrang Dal members disrupted a silent reading session at AUDA Garden, tore books, and clashed with attendees, leaving 8-10 injured; three arrests made, FIRs against 20 including students and organizers.", "Medical access: No specific information on hospitals or ambulances; 8-10 injuries reported from the August 27 clash, but no details on medical treatment or accessibility.", "Legal support: FIRs filed against 20 individuals; demands for withdrawal of charges; no specific legal aid organizations or helplines mentioned in reports."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-11T12:27:36+00:00","level":"high","status":"Following the August 27 disruption of the silent reading session in Vastrapur, participants and student sympathizers have continued to gather in small groups to read Malala Yousafzai and Anne Frank bo"},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:14:09+00:00","level":"high","status":"Following the August 27 disruption of the silent reading session in Vastrapur, participants and student sympathizers have continued to gather in small groups to read Malala Yousafzai and Anne Frank bo"},{"date":"2026-10-13T12:13:59+00:00","level":"high","status":"The follow-up protest in Vastrapur, Ahmedabad, continues to center on the August 27, 2026 disruption of a silent reading session featuring Malala Yousafzai's 'I Am Malala' and Anne Frank's 'The Diary "}]
