    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to the confirmed violence on August 27, 2026, when VHP and Bajrang Dal members attacked a reading session in Vastrapur, injuring 8-10 people and tearing books. Three arrests have been made, but FIRs against 20 individuals indicate ongoing legal proceedings and potential for retaliation. The involvement of organized right-wing groups with a history of confrontational tactics, combined with the political sensitivity of the books' subject matter, creates a high risk of further violence at any follow-up gatherings.",
    "status": "The follow-up protest activity in Vastrapur, Ahmedabad remains centered on the August 27, 2026 attack on a silent reading session at AUDA Garden featuring Malala Yousafzai's memoir and Anne Frank's diary. On that day, members of the VHP and Bajrang Dal allegedly disrupted the gathering, tore books, and injured 8-10 participants. Police arrested three individuals and registered FIRs against 20 people. Civil society groups subsequently held a silent reading protest at Law Garden to assert the 'right to read'. No new incidents or escalations have been reported in the search results since the initial attack and the Law Garden follow-up.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Not specified in search results; no information on deployment numbers, equipment, or road closures in Vastrapur or Law Garden.", "Recent incidents: August 27, 2026: VHP/Bajrang Dal disrupted silent reading at AUDA Garden, Vastrapur; tore books; 8-10 injured; 3 arrested, FIRs against 20.", "Medical access: No details on hospitals, ambulances, or accessibility; injuries reported (8-10) but treatment information unavailable.", "Legal support: 3 arrested, FIRs against 20; no mention of legal aid organizations, helplines, or court interventions."],
