    "name": "Anti-Paper Leak Protest March at Gardanibagh",
    "location": "Gardanibagh area, Patna",
    "cause": "Protesters are demonstrating against repeated question paper leaks in Bihar recruitment exams, demanding systemic reforms and accountability from the BPSC and state government.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains critical because police have repeatedly used force against protesters in Patna, including water cannons and batons during a march from Gandhi Maidan that turned violent. The protest was further inflamed by BPSC Exam Controller Rajesh Kumar Singh's derogatory 'dogs bark' remark, which protesters view as dismissive of paper leak allegations. Detentions have occurred, notably RJD leader Tejashwi Yadav was detained after a march to Lok Bhavan was stopped, showing political figures are also being taken into custody. The protests have spread to multiple districts including Siwan, Chhapra, and Jehanabad, indicating a widening and unresolved standoff. The government has not met core demands such as cancellation of the 70th BPSC exam, sustaining protest momentum and tension.",
    "status": "The Anti-Paper Leak Protest March at Gardanibagh in Patna remains an active and escalating student-led agitation. Hundreds of students and unemployed youth marched from Gandhi Maidan and clashed with police, who used water cannons and batons to stop them. The protest was triggered by BPSC Exam Controller Rajesh Kumar Singh's derogatory 'dogs bark' remark dismissing paper leak claims, which intensified anger. RJD leader Tejashwi Yadav was detained after a march to Lok Bhavan was stopped, and after his release he stated the protest will not stop until the Chief Minister takes responsibility. Rahul Gandhi slammed the Bihar government for weaponising police against students. Despite the BPSC announcing TRE-4 for 32,388 teacher posts with online applications from September 1–30, teacher aspirants continue to protest over unresolved demands including single-tier exams and anti-corruption measures. Protests have also spread to Siwan, Chhapra, and Jehanabad, indicating a widening movement.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Heavy police deployment in Patna, especially at Gandhi Maidan and Gardanibagh; water cannons and batons used to disperse protesters; barricades erected; no official numbers released.", "Recent incidents: On Tuesday, students clashed with police during a massive march in Patna; police used water cannons and batons; RJD leader Tejashwi Yadav was detained after a march to Lok Bhavan was stopped; protests spread to Siwan, Chhapra, and Jehanabad.", "Medical access: No specific information available on hospitals, ambulances, or injuries in the search results.", "Legal support: No specific information available on legal aid organizations, helplines, or court interventions in the search results."],
