    "details": ["Police presence: Specific deployment numbers for the August 28 protest have not been announced; Amaravati region typically sees Andhra Pradesh police and APSP battalions stationed near the Assembly and Secretariat, with barricades and drone surveillance during sessions.", "Recent incidents: No violence or arrests reported for this specific August 28 call; however, CM Naidu's warning against public-life disruption and the ongoing YSRCP teacher recruitment agitation have heightened tensions in Amaravati during the run-up to the Assembly session.", "Medical access: Amaravati is served by government and private hospitals in nearby Vijayawada and Guntur, including Government General Hospital (Guntur) and Vijayawada Government General Hospital; no ambulances have been pre-positioned for this protest and no injuries have been reported.", "Legal support: A.P. JAC Amaravati has its own legal cell and union-affiliated advocates; no detentions have been reported for this call, and no court interventions specific to the August 28 protest have been recorded as of now."],
