    "status": "The app-based cab and bike taxi drivers' protest in Bhubaneswar continued into its third day on August 19, 2026, with drivers taking out a rally from Raj Mahal Square and parking vehicles along Mahatma Gandhi Marg, blocking roads and disrupting traffic in the Master Canteen and railway station areas. The strike turned violent on August 19 when protesters allegedly threw stones at police personnel and vandalised government-run 'Ama' buses at PMG Square. Police detained over 100 individuals and seized vehicles, declaring the protest illegal; reports indicate 25 protesters and 10 police personnel were injured in the face-off. The Odisha government has not yet publicly addressed the drivers' seven-point charter of demands, which includes fair fare regulation, a fare hike, reduced application fees, social security benefits, and fair payment for waiting time. The Odisha Online Drivers United Forum has called for continued agitation, and the situation remains tense with the potential for further escalation if talks do not materialise. The strike has also caused ride-hailing prices to surge in Bhubaneswar due to the disruption of app-based services, and commuters struggled to book rides through state-backed mobility platform Odisha Yatri.",
