    "dangerReason": "The protest turned violent on Wednesday at Lower PMG Square, resulting in 13 police officers injured and 113 arrests, indicating a serious breakdown of order. Police seized 354 vehicles and filed seven FIRs against protesters for violence, property damage, and unlawful assembly, showing a heavy-handed crackdown. The scale of arrests and vehicle seizures, combined with injuries to law enforcement, demonstrates active enforcement and widespread disruption across Bhubaneswar. Although the union apologised on Friday, the situation remains tense with ongoing permit action and the threat of escalation if demands are unmet. The presence of multiple protest locations and the involvement of major app-based platforms (Ola, Uber, Rapido) heighten the risk of further clashes.",
    "status": "The Bhubaneswar app-based drivers' strike, led by the Smart City Online Auto-Taxi Drivers Union, escalated into violence on Wednesday at Lower PMG Square, where Ola, Uber, and Rapido drivers had gathered to press a seven-point charter of demands including fare hikes, reduced application fees, and social security benefits. Clashes with police left 13 officers injured, and Odisha Police subsequently arrested 113 people and seized 354 vehicles across the city. Seven FIRs were filed against protesters for violence, property damage, and unlawful assembly. The crackdown has widened into permit action against the seized vehicles. On Friday, two days after the violence, the drivers' union publicly apologised for the violence. The strike had paralysed app-based transport services across Bhubaneswar, with drivers blocking major intersections including Master Canteen Square, Rajmahal Square, and KIIT Square. The union has threatened to escalate if demands are not met, though the apology suggests a possible de-escalation.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Heavy police deployment at Lower PMG Square, Master Canteen Square, Rajmahal Square, and KIIT Square. Odisha Police conducted arrests and vehicle seizures; 354 vehicles seized. Barricades and road closures likely, though specific equipment not detailed in reports.", "Recent incidents: On Wednesday, protest at Lower PMG Square turned violent, leaving 13 cops injured. Police arrested 113 people and filed seven FIRs for violence, property damage, and unlawful assembly. On Friday, the Smart City Online Auto-Taxi Drivers Union apologised for the violence.", "Medical access: 13 police officers injured in Wednesday's clash; no reports of protester injuries or medical access issues. Hospitals in Bhubaneswar are accessible, but no specific medical support details available.", "Legal support: 113 arrested and forwarded to court; seven FIRs filed. Permit action initiated against seized vehicles. No legal aid organizations or helplines mentioned. Union issued apology, but legal status of detained protesters unclear."],
