    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "The protest turned violent on August 19, 2026, when agitators pelted stones at police, injuring at least 13 police personnel, including the inspector-in-charge of Capital police station. Protesters also vandalised three police vans and over 10 government-run Ama buses. Police arrested 113 people and seized 354 vehicles, with seven FIRs registered at Kharvel Nagar police station. The State transport authority has initiated the process for suspension and cancellation of permits of the auto-rickshaws used to block the main road. The situation remains tense as the strike continues, with no indication of de-escalation.",
    "status": "The strike by app-based cab, auto and bike-taxi drivers in Bhubaneswar, which began on August 17, 2026, turned violent on August 19, 2026, when protesters clashed with police at Master Canteen Square and Station Square. Hundreds of drivers participated, blocking roads and disrupting traffic near the railway station. According to police, 113 people were arrested and 354 vehicles seized, while at least 13 police personnel, including the inspector-in-charge of Capital police station, were injured. Protesters allegedly pelted stones at police and vandalised over 10 government-run 'Ama' buses and three police vans. Seven FIRs were registered at Kharvel Nagar police station, and the State transport authority has initiated suspension and cancellation of permits for auto-rickshaws used to block the main road. On August 21, 2026, the Smart City Online Auto-Taxi Drivers Union issued a public apology for the violence. The strike continues as drivers press their seven-point charter of demands, including a fare hike, reduction in application fees, and social security benefits.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Heavy police deployment at Master Canteen Square, Station Square, and surrounding areas; 113 arrests and 354 vehicles seized; seven FIRs at Kharvel Nagar police station; State transport authority moving to suspend/cancel permits of autos used in roadblocks.", "Recent incidents: On August 19, 2026, protesters pelted stones at police, injuring 13 cops including the Capital PS IIC; over 10 Ama buses and three police vans vandalised; traffic near Station Square disrupted for hours; strike entered third day on August 19 with commuters facing severe inconvenience.", "Medical access: No specific reports of protester injuries or ambulance access issues; 13 police personnel injured and treated; hospitals in Bhubaneswar remain accessible though protest areas may cause delays.", "Legal support: Smart City Online Auto-Taxi Drivers Union issued a public apology on August 21, 2026, for the violence; no known legal helplines or court interventions reported; 113 arrested individuals face charges under multiple FIRs; permit suspension/cancellation proceedings initiated by State transport authority."],
