    "cause": "Students are protesting against the repeated leak of question papers for state-level examinations, demanding a thorough investigation, cancellation of compromised exams, and strict action against the leak syndicate. The protest has escalated following a similar demonstration in Bihar where police used water cannons.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to the tense standoff between protesters and police at Lower PMG Square, where barricades have been reinforced and additional personnel deployed. Permission for a march to the State Secretariat was denied, increasing the risk of confrontation. The gherao of Union Minister Dharmendra Pradhan's residence by NSUI activists shows the protest is targeting high-profile locations, which could lead to clashes. While no violence has been reported in Bhubaneswar, the use of water cannon by police in a similar protest in Bihar on August 25 has been cited by organizers, indicating a potential for escalation. The involvement of multiple student and political organizations, including SFI, NSUI, AISF, and Youth Congress, broadens the scope and intensity of the agitation.",
    "status": "Student and political organizations continue to protest in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors, with gatherings centered at Lower PMG Square. The Odisha Youth Congress held a torch rally (mashal rally) in Bhubaneswar targeting the BJP government over over 3,000 errors in school textbooks and exam paper leaks. Reuters reported that police in Bihar used water cannon and detained dozens of protesters attempting a march, and a separate report indicated that police used water cannons to disperse thousands of youth protesters marching on the state legislature in India. The protests have drawn participation from multiple groups including NSUI, Youth Congress, and SFI, with Union Minister Dharmendra Pradhan reportedly joining around 1,500 students. The state government's offer of a committee review has been rejected by protesters who demand immediate cancellation of compromised exams and strict action against leak syndicates. The agitation remains ongoing with no confirmed end date, and similar protests have occurred in other states.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Barricades reinforced at Lower PMG Square; additional personnel deployed; march to State Secretariat denied permission; no water cannons or tear gas reported in Bhubaneswar.", "Recent incidents: Odisha Youth Congress torch rally in Bhubaneswar over textbook errors and exam leaks; NSUI activists gheraoed Union Minister Dharmendra Pradhan's residence; no violence reported in Bhubaneswar; water cannon and detentions occurred in Bihar on August 25.", "Medical access: No injuries reported in Bhubaneswar protests; hospitals nearby not specified; ambulances not mentioned as on site.", "Legal support: No legal aid organizations or helplines mentioned; legal status of detained protesters in Bihar unknown; no court interventions reported."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-09-10T12:10:04+00:00","level":"high","status":"The protest at Lower PMG Square has been ongoing for several days, with student unions from various colleges and universities gathering in the afternoon. On August 25, police in Bhubaneswar reinforced"},{"date":"2026-09-11T00:09:23+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student unions and youth organisations have been gathering at Lower PMG Square in Bhubaneswar over repeated leaks of state-level examination question papers, demanding a thorough probe, cancellation o"},{"date":"2026-09-11T12:09:15+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student unions and youth organisations continue to gather at Lower PMG Square in Bhubaneswar over repeated leaks of state-level examination question papers, demanding a thorough probe, cancellation of"},{"date":"2026-09-15T00:10:31+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student unions, youth organisations and political outfits continue to agitate in Bhubaneswar over repeated leaks of state-level examination question papers, demanding a thorough probe, cancellation of"},{"date":"2026-10-02T12:15:42+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student protests against alleged NEET-UG 2026 paper leaks continue at Lower PMG Square in Bhubaneswar, with hundreds of students gathering for torchlight rallies and marches. The Students' Federation "},{"date":"2026-10-06T00:09:06+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student protests in Bhubaneswar over the alleged NEET-UG 2026 paper leak have continued as torchlight rallies and marches, with large participation from Youth Congress, NSUI, and SFI. Hundreds of stud"},{"date":"2026-10-10T00:03:50+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student protests in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors have continued, with hundreds of students gathering at Lower PMG Square and conducting torchlight rallies and m"},{"date":"2026-10-11T00:06:26+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student and political organizations continue to protest in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors, with gatherings centered at Lower PMG Square. The Odisha Youth Congress"},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:14:23+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student and political organizations continue to protest in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors, with gatherings centered at Lower PMG Square. The Odisha Youth Congress"},{"date":"2026-10-12T12:10:51+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student and political organizations continue to protest in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors, with gatherings centered at Lower PMG Square. The Odisha Youth Congress"},{"date":"2026-10-13T00:17:23+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student and political organizations continue to protest in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors, with gatherings centered at Lower PMG Square. The Odisha Youth Congress"},{"date":"2026-10-16T00:15:18+00:00","level":"high","status":"Student and political organizations continue to protest in Bhubaneswar over alleged examination paper leaks and textbook errors, with gatherings centered at Lower PMG Square. The Odisha Youth Congress"}]
