    "name": "KSU-Youth Congress March vs SFI-DYFI Clashes at Kerala University Hostel",
    "location": "Kerala University Men's Hostel premises and surrounding roads, Palayam, Thiruvananthapuram",
    "cause": "KSU and Youth Congress activists marched against the Chief Minister and alleged hostel-related grievances, while SFI and DYFI activists countered them. Stones and flaming torches were exchanged between the two groups near the Kerala University Men's Hostel, escalating into a major campus-political confrontation.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "The September 29-30, 2026 clash involved stones, beer bottles, and flaming torches exchanged between KSU/Youth Congress and SFI/DYFI activists near the Kerala University Men's Hostel in Palayam, Thiruvananthapuram. Police registered two separate cases against 160 activists (80 from each side), indicating a large-scale confrontation and mass bookings. The violence triggered retaliatory attacks, including stone-throwing that shattered a window at the District Congress Committee office near Bakery Junction. SFI's call for a statewide protest at educational institutions on Thursday raises the risk of further flashpoints. The use of weapons-like objects (stones, bottles, torches) and the mass case registration justify a critical danger level.",
    "status": "The KSU-Youth Congress march against the Union government and Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar near the Kerala University Men's Hostel in Palayam, Thiruvananthapuram, escalated into a violent clash with SFI-DYFI activists on September 29-30, 2026. Stones, beer bottles, and flaming torches were exchanged between the two groups, and several people were injured. Police registered two separate cases on Thursday, October 1, 2026, against 160 activists — 80 from KSU/Youth Congress and 80 from SFI/DYFI — in connection with the violence. The clash reportedly began after stones were allegedly thrown from inside the Kerala University men's hostel premises at the Youth Congress protest march. Kerala Chief Minister V D Satheesan condemned the clash and warned of stern action against attempts to disrupt peace. SFI has announced a statewide protest at educational institutions, raising the risk of further flashpoints. Police have stepped up deployment around the university campus and Palayam junction to prevent renewed clashes.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Heavy deployment around Kerala University campus and Palayam junction; tear gas used during clash; 160 activists booked in two cases; security stepped up to prevent renewed violence.", "Recent incidents: Sept 29-30, 2026 clash with stones, beer bottles, flaming torches; several injured; DCC office window shattered near Bakery Junction; 160 booked Oct 1; SFI announced statewide protests.", "Medical access: Several injured reported; no specific hospital details available; ambulances not mentioned; campus area accessible but tense.", "Legal support: 160 activists booked in two cases (80 KSU/YC, 80 SFI/DYFI); arrests made; no specific legal aid organizations mentioned; CM warned of stern action."],
