    "status": "The Samyukta Kisan Morcha has announced a week-long protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border running from September 1 to September 7, 2025, with farmers gathering at the border crossing and adjacent entry points. Chandigarh Traffic Police issued an advisory on August 30 announcing traffic diversions starting August 31 to manage the expected congestion, redirecting vehicles away from the Mohali border route. Organizers claim thousands of farmers from across Punjab will participate in rotating shifts throughout the week. Police have deployed additional personnel at the border and set up barricades, but no clashes have been reported as of the protest's opening days. The SKM plans to continue the blockade through September 7 unless the government opens negotiations on MSP and debt relief demands.",
    "details": ["Chandigarh Traffic Police deployed officers at all major entry points from Mohali; barricades placed at Phase 8 border, Sector 48-49 crossing, and Airport Road; diversions announced from Aug 31 via official advisory.", "No violent incidents reported in the first days of the Sept 1-7 protest; traffic snarls reported across tricity; previous Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protests at same border saw tear gas and water cannon use by police.", "PGIMER Chandigarh and Government Medical College Sector 32 are nearest major hospitals to the border protest site; ambulances not confirmed on-site; emergency access routes via Sector 48-49 kept partially open per police advisory.", "SKM legal team and farmer union lawyers monitoring the protest; no detentions reported as of early September; protesters operating under announced peaceful blockade framework; Punjab and Haryana HC has previously affirmed right to peaceful protest."],
