    "status": "The Bandi Sikh March, backed by the SGPC and Qaumi Insaaf Morcha, remains an active and tense mobilisation centred on the Parade Ground in Sector 17, Chandigarh, with a planned march route towards the Punjab Raj Bhavan. Search intelligence confirms that Chandigarh Police deployed tear gas shells and water cannons to prevent Qaumi Insaaf Morcha activists from heading towards the Punjab Chief Minister's residence, and that the underlying Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest has been running since January 7, 2023 at the Chandigarh–Mohali border. A video allegedly showing jailed extremist Jagtar Singh Hawara appealing for peace surfaced ahead of the August 15 march, and Sikh bodies called a Punjab bandh on August 21 with planned rail blockades. A large religious and political gathering was also held at Hawara Kalan village in Khamano of Fatehgarh Sahib district on a Saturday, demanding the release of Bandi Singhs. The SGPC has communicated to the Centre a list of nine Sikh prisoners, including six convicted for the assassination of former CM Beant Singh, while 22 Sikh prisoners remain behind bars. Organisers have not announced any conclusion, so the agitation continues.",
