    "name": "Qaumi Insaaf Morcha Punjab Bandh for Release of Sikh Prisoners",
    "location": "Statewide across Punjab, with major gatherings at Chandigarh's Sector 17 Plaza and Punjab Raj Bhawan",
    "cause": "Demanding the immediate release of Sikh prisoners, including those convicted in 1984 anti-Sikh riots cases and alleged extremists, ahead of the 'Bandi Sikh' march in Chandigarh on August 15.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level is high due to confirmed clashes between protesters and police at the Chandigarh-Mohali border on August 21, 2026, where tear gas shells and water cannons were deployed to disperse crowds attempting to breach barricades. The bandh caused widespread disruption, with markets shut in parts of Punjab and highways blocked, indicating significant mobilization. The protest was triggered by alleged police force during the August 15 march and subsequent FIRs against Morcha members, suggesting ongoing grievances and potential for further escalation. Security remains heightened at the Chandigarh-Mohali border, and the situation is tense but currently contained.",
    "status": "The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha observed a seven-hour Punjab Bandh on August 21, 2026, from 7 AM to 2 PM, demanding the release of Sikh prisoners ('Bandi Singhs'). The bandh evoked a mixed response, with markets shut in parts of Punjab, highways blocked, and transport disrupted. At the Chandigarh-Mohali border, protesters attempted to breach police barricades while marching towards Punjab Lok Bhawan, prompting police to use tear gas shells and water cannons to disperse them. Security remains tight at the border, with government schools remaining open and traffic affected from 7 AM to 2 PM. The Shiromani Akali Dal, led by Sukhbir Singh Badal, supports the demand for the release of 'bandi Singhs' but has not explicitly supported the bandh. No immediate future plans have been announced by the Morcha.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Tight security at Chandigarh-Mohali border with barricades; tear gas shells and water cannons used on August 21; traffic affected from 7 AM to 2 PM; government schools open.", "Recent incidents: On August 21, 2026, Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protesters attempted to breach police barricades at Chandigarh-Mohali border; police responded with tear gas and water cannons; markets shut and highways blocked across Punjab.", "Medical access: No specific information available in search results regarding hospitals, ambulances, or injuries.", "Legal support: No specific information available in search results regarding legal organizations, helplines, or court interventions."],
