    "status": "Guwahati-based cab operators have been blocking Meghalaya-bound traffic at Jorabat and Khanapara, the main entry points to Meghalaya, since the Shillong violence erupted. The Assam State Driver Association suspended all Guwahati–Shillong car services, and the blockade has stranded numerous passengers on the route. Assam and Meghalaya Chief Ministers issued a joint peace appeal on August 20, 2026, urging restraint, while ministers from both states prepared to meet to resolve the impasse. Police are deployed at the blockade sites to prevent escalation, but the cab operators have not yet announced when they will lift the blockade.",
