    "status": "The Assam State Driver Association has suspended all Guwahati–Shillong and Shillong–Guwahati car services following alleged violence against Assam-registered vehicles and drivers during rioting in Shillong. The 3-day road blockade on National Highway-27 at Jorabat on the Assam side was suspended on Saturday evening after Assam Minister Atul Bora visited the protest site, and the border route at Jorabat has since reopened. However, taxi services remain disrupted, with the association deciding to keep the agitation on hold until a Special Investigation Team is constituted. Meghalaya taxi associations have also halted Shillong–Guwahati services citing safety fears, and Assam-registered vehicles attempting the route have been turned back at Umiam and Byrnihat. The North-East Petroleum Mazdoor union has additionally suspended fuel and LPG transport from Assam to Meghalaya over safety concerns, widening the economic impact. Drivers are demanding written safety guarantees and compensation for damages before resuming operations, while hundreds of passengers remain stranded with no alternative transport arrangements announced.",
