    "name": "J&K-Wide August 5 'Black Day' Protest Call by Mehbooba Mufti",
    "location": "PDP headquarters, Srinagar; protests called across all districts of Jammu and Kashmir",
    "cause": "Mehbooba Mufti has called for J&K-wide protests on August 5 to mark the anniversary of the abrogation of Article 370, demanding restoration of the erstwhile state's special status and advocating 'meaningful engagement' as the only way forward.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "August 5 anniversaries in Srinagar have historically seen heavy security deployment, preventive detentions of party leaders, and clashes between protesters and police. In previous years, National Conference and PDP workers have been detained preemptively, and Section 144-style restrictions have been imposed across the city. The combination of a ruling-party (NC) protest at its headquarters and a PDP-led call for district-wide demonstrations raises the risk of multiple flashpoints and mass detentions on a single day.",
    "status": "Mehbooba Mufti has publicly urged J&K-wide protests on August 5, framing the day as a 'Black Day' and reiterating that dialogue and restoration of Article 370 are prerequisites for lasting peace. The PDP has not yet specified the exact gathering point in Srinagar, but the call covers all districts, meaning simultaneous demonstrations are expected. Police are anticipated to impose restrictions around sensitive areas including the PDP headquarters and Lal Chowk. Party workers are expected to attempt marches despite likely prohibitory orders, and detentions of senior leaders are probable. The situation remains fluid with the government yet to announce its formal security posture for the day.",
    "details": ["Heavy police and CRPF deployment expected around PDP headquarters, Lal Chowk, and district entry points; barricades and concertina wire likely on major roads.", "In past August 5 observances, NC and PDP leaders including sitting MLAs have been placed under preventive detention; workers have been stopped at barricades and bussed away.", "SMHS Hospital and Shri Maharaja Hari Singh Hospital are the nearest major medical facilities; ambulances are typically stationed near protest zones during August 5 events.", "PDP legal cell and J&K High Court Bar Association lawyers typically represent detained workers; habeas corpus petitions have been filed in past years for preventive detentions."],
    "trendHistory": []
