    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to the heavy security deployment, including police, Army, and CRPF personnel, and the police warning of legal action against unauthorised protests. An FIR was filed against Iltija Mufti after an alleged assault during a protest, and she was summoned by police, indicating active legal consequences for participants. The PDP alleged police assault, suggesting physical confrontation occurred. The sensitive nature of the Article 370 anniversary and the history of mass detentions and communication blackouts elevate the risk. The protests are ongoing with multiple parties involved, and the situation remains tense with potential for further escalation.",
    "status": "The seventh anniversary of the abrogation of Article 370 saw multiple protests across Srinagar, with the PDP holding a candlelight march at its party headquarters on August 4, led by party chief Mehbooba Mufti. The National Conference also observed August 5 as 'Black Day' with protests at its headquarters in Srinagar and across all districts. Security was tightened across Jammu and Kashmir with heavy deployment of police, Army, and CRPF personnel ahead of the protests. Police issued an advisory warning of legal action against unauthorised protests, marches, or rallies without prior permission. An FIR was registered against Iltija Mufti following an alleged assault during a Srinagar protest, and she was summoned to appear at Police Station Kothibagh on August 7. The PDP alleged police assault and political repression. Organizers have indicated plans to continue symbolic demonstrations and coordinate with other regional parties for future anniversaries.",
