    "name": "Environmentalists Protest Outside NHAI Office Over Rishikesh Highway Tree Felling",
    "location": "NHAI Regional Office, Dehradun",
    "cause": "Citizens, environmentalists, and youth are protesting outside the NHAI Regional Office against the felling of trees for the Rishikesh highway widening project. They demand an environmental impact review and alternative alignment to protect the green cover.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The situation remains high-risk due to escalating detentions ahead of a Supreme Court hearing and fresh tree felling at Saat Mod despite a High Court order, which has triggered renewed protests. The involvement of thousands in Rishikesh and sustained demonstrations over multiple days, including 'Black Harela' observances, indicates growing momentum. While no mass violence has been reported, the sensitive location of the NHAI office and the defiance of court orders elevate the potential for confrontation. The High Court's dismissal of the contempt petition and its refusal to stay the project further heighten tensions between protesters and authorities.",
    "status": "Residents, environmentalists, and youth have continued protesting outside the NHAI Regional Office in Dehradun and at 'Saat Mod' against the felling of 4,369 trees for the Bhaniyawala–Jolly Grant–Rishikesh highway widening project. The protests, which have persisted for over a week, prompted Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami to halt tree felling and order stakeholder talks. However, fresh felling was reported at Saat Mod reserve forest despite a Uttarakhand High Court order halting the project, leading to renewed local protests. Detentions have increased ahead of a Supreme Court hearing, and the Uttarakhand High Court dismissed a contempt petition against the NHAI project director, effectively clearing the way for the project. Organizers plan to continue until an environmental impact review and alternative alignment are ordered.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Not specified in search results; likely deployed at NHAI office and Saat Mod given detentions, but exact numbers and equipment unconfirmed.", "Recent incidents: Fresh tree felling at Saat Mod reserve forest despite High Court order; detentions increased ahead of Supreme Court hearing; no violence reported.", "Medical access: No information available in search results.", "Legal support: Environmentalists filed contempt petition against NHAI project director; Uttarakhand High Court dismissed it and refused to stay project; Supreme Court hearing pending."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-06T00:15:28+00:00","level":"moderate","status":"A powerful wave of anger was witnessed in Dehradun as citizens, environmentalists, and youth gathered outside the NHAI Regional Office to protest against tree felling for the Rishikesh highway project"},{"date":"2026-10-10T12:08:47+00:00","level":"moderate","status":"Citizens, environmentalists, and youth have been protesting outside the NHAI Regional Office in Dehradun against the felling of 4,369 trees for the Bhaniyawala–Jolly Grant–Rishikesh highway wideni"},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:04:36+00:00","level":"high","status":"Residents, environmentalists, and youth have been protesting outside the NHAI Regional Office in Dehradun and at 'Saat Mod' against the felling of 4,369 trees for the Bhaniyawala–Jolly Grant–Rishi"},{"date":"2026-10-13T00:15:08+00:00","level":"high","status":"Residents, environmentalists, and youth have continued protesting outside the NHAI Regional Office in Dehradun and at 'Saat Mod' against the felling of 4,369 trees for the Bhaniyawala–Jolly Grant–"},{"date":"2026-10-16T00:12:22+00:00","level":"high","status":"Residents, environmentalists, and youth have continued protesting outside the NHAI Regional Office in Dehradun and at 'Saat Mod' against the felling of 4,369 trees for the Bhaniyawala–Jolly Grant–"}]
