    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to the tense standoff between job aspirants and police near the Uttarakhand Secretariat in Dehradun, with barricades erected and additional forces deployed. Clashes were reported when protesters attempted to march toward government buildings, leading to several detentions and raising the risk of further confrontations. The involvement of large, angry youth crowds near sensitive government installations, combined with the protesters' determination to continue until their demands are met, creates a volatile environment where escalation remains possible. Although the CM's visit and promise of a CBI probe may have de-escalated the specific paper leak protest, the broader recruitment-delay agitation and other ongoing protests (nursing, TET) indicate sustained unrest. The lack of confirmed mass violence or serious injuries in the latest reports prevents a critical rating, but the potential for injury or further detentions is significant.",
    "status": "Hundreds of government job aspirants under the banner of Uttarakhand Berozgar Sangh remain gathered at Parade Ground in Dehradun, continuing their agitation over prolonged recruitment delays by UKSSSC and other bodies. On 21 July, a large number of unemployed youth marched and held a dharna in Dehradun, raising slogans against both the Union and State Governments. The most recent search results indicate that Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami visited Parade Ground and interacted with the protesting youth, and in a related development, paper leak protests were called off after the CM promised a CBI probe. However, the current status of the specific recruitment-delay protest is unclear, as some reports suggest the agitation may have been suspended following the CBI probe assurance, while others show ongoing protests by different groups (nursing aspirants, primary teachers) in Dehradun. No new incidents of mass violence or serious injuries have been confirmed in the latest reports. Protest leaders had earlier announced plans to continue until fresh job notifications are issued, but the CBI probe promise may have addressed a key demand. The situation appears to be evolving, with a mix of de-escalation signals and continued unrest among other aspirant groups.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Barricades erected around Parade Ground and the Secretariat area in Dehradun; additional forces deployed to prevent protesters from marching toward government offices. Specific numbers not provided in search results.", "Recent incidents: On 21 July, a large number of unemployed youth under Uttarakhand Berozgar Sangh marched and held a dharna in Dehradun, raising slogans against Union and State Governments. Clashes were reported when protesters attempted to march toward government buildings, leading to several detentions. No confirmed injuries.", "Medical access: No specific information available on hospitals nearby, ambulances on site, or injuries reported in the latest search results.", "Legal support: No specific information available on organizations/lawyers involved, helplines, legal status of detained protesters, or court interventions in the latest search results."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-09-15T12:07:35+00:00","level":"high","status":"Hundreds of government job aspirants have gathered at Parade Ground in Dehradun, demanding immediate declaration of pending recruitment results and a probe into paper leaks. The protest follows a larg"},{"date":"2026-10-06T00:15:23+00:00","level":"high","status":"Hundreds of government job aspirants remain gathered at Parade Ground in Dehradun, continuing their protest against prolonged delays in recruitment results by the Uttarakhand Subordinate Services Sele"},{"date":"2026-10-10T00:06:11+00:00","level":"high","status":"Hundreds of government job aspirants remain gathered at Parade Ground in Dehradun, continuing their agitation against prolonged delays in recruitment results by the Uttarakhand Subordinate Services Se"},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:08:45+00:00","level":"high","status":"Hundreds of government job aspirants remain gathered at Parade Ground in Dehradun, continuing their agitation against prolonged delays in recruitment results by the Uttarakhand Subordinate Services Se"}]
