    "location": "Panaji city area, including Azad Maidan and surrounding protest sites; specific detention location not fully disclosed by police",
    "cause": "Protesters displayed 'Free Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam' placards during a solidarity protest, demanding the release of jailed student activist Umar Khalid and Sharjeel Imam. Goa Police detained individuals and filed an FIR against unknown supporters and protesters for unlawful assembly and organizing without prior permission.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high due to multiple detentions and an active FIR against protesters. Goa Police detained at least three individuals—one man for displaying a 'Free Umar Khalid' placard and two youths for expressing support—with reports of scuffles and heated arguments during the detentions. The FIR for unlawful assembly and organizing without permission indicates a formal legal escalation, and police have grilled organizers over funding and intent, suggesting intensified surveillance. The detentions have sparked protests demanding release, raising the potential for further confrontations. While no mass violence or injuries have been confirmed, the tense standoff and ongoing investigation justify a high rating.",
    "status": "The Free Umar Khalid solidarity protest in Panaji remains active as of mid-October 2026, with Goa Police continuing enforcement actions against participants. On Saturday evening, a man was detained for questioning after displaying a placard reading 'Free Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam, Bhima Koregaon 16' during a solidarity protest in the Panaji city area. Separately, two youths were detained for allegedly expressing support for Umar Khalid during celebrations linked to a CJP protest. The detentions sparked immediate protests demanding the release of those held, with scuffles and heated arguments reported during the police action. An FIR has been filed against unknown supporters and protesters for unlawful assembly and organizing without prior permission. Police have also grilled organizers, including Amreen Shaikh, who was summoned to Panaji Police Station on July 29 for questioning over NEET protests. Most recently, on October 13, 2026, Goa Police denied permission to Cockroach Janata Party protesters to gather inside Azad Maidan in Panaji on Sunday, citing 'past history' of support to Umar Khalid as the reason. The investigation appears to be widening, with police probing funding and intent behind the placards, and further questioning or arrests may follow.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Goa Police detained a man on Saturday evening in Panaji for displaying a 'Free Umar Khalid' placard; two others were detained for similar support during a CJP protest celebration. Police denied permission for a CJP gathering at Azad Maidan on Sunday, citing past Umar Khalid support. Specific deployment numbers and equipment not disclosed.", "Recent incidents: On Saturday evening, one man was detained for a 'Free Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam, Bhima Koregaon 16' placard; two youths were detained for expressing support during CJP celebrations. Scuffles and heated arguments occurred during detentions. An FIR was filed against unknown supporters for unlawful assembly and organizing without permission. On October 13, 2026, police denied permission for a CJP protest at Azad Maidan.", "Medical access: No injuries or medical access issues have been reported in available search results. No ambulances or hospitals mentioned. Information on medical access is currently unavailable.", "Legal support: An FIR has been filed against unknown supporters and protesters for unlawful assembly and organizing without prior permission. Organizer Amreen Shaikh was summoned to Panaji Police Station on July 29 for questioning over NEET protests. No specific legal aid organizations or helplines mentioned in search results."],
