    "status": "The Free Umar Khalid Solidarity Protest in Panaji, Goa, saw activists displaying placards reading 'Free Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam, Bhima Koregaon 16' in the central Panaji area near the police station. On a Saturday evening, Goa Police detained two individuals, including Mohammad Danish, for questioning to prevent law-and-order problems. The placard display drew attention from counter-protesters, including BJP Yuva Morcha members, leading to a tense standoff before police intervened. Goa Police later issued a 240-point questionnaire to at least two protesters who had participated in a July 24 demonstration in Mapusa, asking questions such as 'Did you shout Free Umar Khalid slogan?' and 'Who financed the protest?'. The Bombay High Court, in a special Sunday sitting, ordered the release of seven Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) members detained in connection with the protest. Goa Police denied permission to CJP protesters to gather inside Azad Maidan in Panaji on Sunday, citing 'past history' and support to Umar Khalid as reasons. Organizers have not announced any follow-up actions, but solidarity groups may attempt similar demonstrations.",
