    "status": "The CPI(M)-led Left Front launched its statewide 'Jail Bharo' agitation on August 10, 2026, with thousands of activists gathering at the state party headquarters in Melarmath, Agartala, and at district offices across Tripura. During the Agartala agitation, Left activists clashed with police, and former Chief Minister Manik Sarkar along with the CPI(M) State Secretary were detained. On August 25, CPI(M) General Secretary M.A. Baby addressed a public meeting in Agartala, claiming the BJP government was in its 'last days'. On August 26, Leader of the Opposition Jitendra Chaudhury alleged that democratic rights have been curtailed under BJP rule and warned that those involved in attacks would not be spared. The Tripura government has ordered a freeze on the collection of inflated power bills following widespread public anger over smart meters and high electricity charges, but has not responded to the broader demands. The CPI(M) has announced that further phased agitations and mass deputations will continue in the coming weeks.",
