    "status": "Small groups of activists, student leaders, and civil liberties advocates have been gathering in Agartala's activist circles and near the Press Club since the Delhi Police Crime Branch confirmed it is probing a premeditated angle in the CJP July protest violence. Participation remains in the dozens rather than hundreds, with organizers coordinating largely through messaging groups and informal meetings rather than public rallies. Tripura Police have not issued any formal statement on whether Agartala activists are named in the Delhi probe, but local intelligence units are reportedly monitoring social media activity. Organizers say they plan to hold a public meeting and possibly a silent march if any Agartala-based activist is summoned by Delhi Police. No detentions have been reported in Agartala so far in connection with this solidarity mobilization.",
