    "name": "Enumerator Training Disruption Protest in Imphal",
    "location": "Census enumerator training centres across Imphal West and Imphal East districts, including near DC Office complex, Imphal",
    "cause": "Protesters are disrupting Census enumerator training sessions to demand that the National Register of Citizens (NRC) be updated before the Census exercise proceeds, arguing that enumeration without NRC verification will legitimize illegal immigrants.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The situation remains high-risk due to the active disruption of government training programmes, the imposition of a 48-hour statewide bandh, and the involvement of large numbers of protesters including students and women's groups. The cancellation and deferral of Census training in Imphal West and at GM Hall indicate the protesters' ability to halt official proceedings, creating a tense standoff with authorities. While no mass arrests or violent clashes have been reported in the latest updates, the previous assessment noted tear gas dispersal at New Checkon, suggesting police willingness to use force if necessary. The bandh and government office boycott raise the potential for economic disruption and confrontations, and the involvement of Meira Paibi groups adds to the mobilisation capacity. The lack of reported injuries or detentions in the current intelligence keeps the level from being critical, but the ongoing disruption and planned escalation warrant a high danger level.",
    "status": "The protest against the Census without NRC updation continues across Imphal, with the Joint Forum for Delimitation (JFD) and student groups disrupting enumerator training programmes at multiple centres. A three-day training programme at GM Hall in Imphal was cancelled, and the Manipur government has deferred training in Imphal West district following protests. The JFD has called a 48-hour Manipur bandh, and Meira Paibi women's groups have held rallies across Imphal, while teachers deployed as enumerators are caught between official orders and protest pressure. Protesters, numbering in the hundreds, have gathered at training venues and government offices, including Lok Bhavan, where JFD members thronged and student wings disrupted proceedings. Police have been deployed but have not resorted to mass arrests, instead attempting to manage the situation. The protesters plan to continue disrupting Census-related activities until the NRC updation demand is met, with further mobilisation through student networks and Meira Paibi groups. The government has ordered closure of all educational institutions from August 20 to 23 amid the shutdown.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Police have been deployed at training venues and government offices including Lok Bhavan, but no mass arrests or violent dispersal reported; exact numbers and equipment not specified in available reports.", "Recent incidents: Three-day Census enumerator training at GM Hall cancelled; training in Imphal West deferred; JFD members thronged Lok Bhavan and student wing disrupted training programme; 48-hour Manipur bandh called; Meira Paibi rallies held across Imphal; educational institutions closed August 20-23.", "Medical access: No reports of injuries or medical access issues in current intelligence; hospitals and ambulances not mentioned.", "Legal support: No information available on legal support, detentions, or court interventions in current reports."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-11T04:18:33+00:00","level":"high","status":"As of August 19, 2026, student groups and JFD activists have disrupted Census enumerator training programmes at multiple centres in Imphal, forcing suspension of official proceedings. The protesters, "},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:22:30+00:00","level":"high","status":"As of August 19, 2026, student groups and JFD activists have disrupted Census enumerator training programmes at multiple centres in Imphal, forcing suspension of official proceedings. The protesters, "},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:13:34+00:00","level":"high","status":"As of the latest reports, the agitation against the Census without NRC updation continues to intensify across Imphal, with the Joint Forum for Delimitation (JFD) and student groups disrupting enumerat"},{"date":"2026-10-12T12:17:28+00:00","level":"high","status":"The agitation against the Census without NRC updation continues across Imphal, with the Joint Forum for Delimitation (JFD) and student groups disrupting enumerator training programmes at multiple cent"},{"date":"2026-10-13T12:16:02+00:00","level":"high","status":"The protest against the Census without NRC updation continues across Imphal, with the Joint Forum for Delimitation (JFD) and student groups disrupting enumerator training programmes at multiple centre"},{"date":"2026-10-14T00:20:50+00:00","level":"high","status":"The protest against the Census without NRC updation continues across Imphal, with the Joint Forum for Delimitation (JFD) and student groups disrupting enumerator training programmes at multiple centre"}]
