    "cause": "Protesters are demanding that the National Register of Citizens (NRC) be updated before the upcoming Census is conducted in Manipur. The strike is a continuation of the broader movement against Census preparations without a prior NRC exercise, driven by concerns over illegal immigration from Myanmar and Bangladesh.",
    "dangerLevel": "high",
    "dangerReason": "The strike has shut down markets, educational institutions, and business establishments across all five valley districts, paralysing normal life for a second consecutive day. The Manipur government's order to close all educational institutions from August 20 to 23 signals official recognition of an escalating and disruptive situation. The Governor's emergency travel to New Delhi to brief the Union Home Minister indicates the state apparatus views the agitation as serious. Previous JFD protests in Imphal have drawn tear gas dispersal by security forces, establishing a pattern of forceful police response to NRC-related agitation. The indefinite nature of the strike and involvement of multiple CSOs raise the risk of confrontations, particularly if protesters attempt to enforce shutdowns at key commercial hubs or block national highways.",
    "status": "The valley-wide shutdown strike demanding an NRC update before Census operations continued into its second day across Imphal West, Imphal East, Thoubal, Bishnupur, and Kakching districts, with markets and business establishments in Imphal city remaining shut. The strike, called by the Joint Forum for Democracy (JFD) and backed by multiple civil society organisations, has paralysed normal life in the valley districts even as the Centre and the Manipur High Court deferred Census-related proceedings. The Manipur government ordered the closure of all educational institutions across the state from August 20 to 23 in response to the escalating agitation. Governor Ajay Bhalla travelled to New Delhi to meet Union Home Minister Amit Shah and brief the Centre on the situation in Manipur. Organisers have indicated the agitation will continue until the government commits to an NRC update before Census operations begin. No large-scale clashes have been reported in the available search intelligence for the second day.",
    "details": ["Police presence: No specific police deployment numbers or equipment details were available in the search results. Security forces are presumed to be deployed across the five valley districts given the shutdown, but exact locations, barricade placements, or road closures are not confirmed.", "Recent incidents: No large-scale clashes, injuries, or arrests were reported in the available search intelligence for the second day of the strike. The agitation remains disruptive but has not escalated into violence according to the sources reviewed.", "Medical access: No information on hospital accessibility, ambulance availability, or protest-related injuries was present in the search results. This remains unverified.", "Legal support: No legal aid organisations, helplines, or court interventions specific to detained protesters were mentioned in the search results. The Manipur High Court's deferment of Census proceedings is noted, but no direct legal support for protesters is confirmed."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-11T04:18:33+00:00","level":"high","status":"Normal life was severely affected across Imphal and the four other valley districts on the second day of the strike on August 19, 2026, with markets, educational institutions, and business establishme"},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:22:24+00:00","level":"high","status":"Normal life was severely affected across Imphal and the four other valley districts on the second day of the strike on August 19, 2026, with markets, educational institutions, and business establishme"},{"date":"2026-10-12T12:17:22+00:00","level":"high","status":"The valley-wide shutdown strike over the demand for an NRC update before Census operations continued into its second day across Imphal West, Imphal East, Thoubal, Bishnupur, and Kakching districts, wi"},{"date":"2026-10-13T12:15:56+00:00","level":"high","status":"The valley-wide shutdown strike demanding an NRC update before Census operations continued into its second day across Imphal West, Imphal East, Thoubal, Bishnupur, and Kakching districts, with markets"}]
