    "dangerReason": "The situation remains tense as the second day of the 48-hour JFD strike on August 19, 2026, has shut down markets, educational institutions and businesses across Imphal and surrounding valley districts, with strike enforcers actively ensuring compliance. The Manipur government's order closing all schools and colleges for three days from August 20, 2026, signals that authorities expect the disruption and tensions to persist beyond the strike period. Previous JFD protests in Imphal have been met with tear gas dispersal by police at New Checkon, indicating a pattern of confrontational policing that could recur. The strike has also disrupted enumerator training sessions, raising friction between organisers and government authorities pushing ahead with Census preparations. No fresh reports of violence, mass detentions or injuries have emerged in the current intelligence, but the combination of enforced shutdowns, heavy police deployment and an unresolved standoff keeps the risk level elevated.",
    "status": "The 48-hour valley-wide strike called by the Joint Forum for Democratic Struggle (JFD) over its demand that the National Register of Citizens be updated before the upcoming Census paralysed normal life across Manipur's valley districts, with widespread public support reported on the second day. Markets including Ima Keithel, Paona Bazar and Thangal Bazar, along with educational institutions and business establishments, remained shut across Imphal West and Imphal East. JFD volunteers continued picketing at key intersections to enforce the shutdown, while police were deployed at strategic locations to monitor the situation. In a significant escalation of the official response, the Manipur government ordered the closure of all schools and colleges for three days from August 20, 2026, citing the widespread protests. The strike is scheduled to conclude after 48 hours, but JFD has indicated that further agitation, including signature campaigns and mass mobilisation, will continue if the government does not respond to its demand.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Police were deployed at strategic locations across Imphal West and Imphal East to monitor the strike, while JFD volunteers maintained pickets at key intersections to enforce the shutdown. Specific deployment numbers, equipment such as barricades or water cannons, and any road closures were not detailed in available reports.", "Recent incidents: On August 19, 2026, the second day of the 48-hour strike, markets including Ima Keithel, Paona Bazar and Thangal Bazar were shuttered and normal life was paralysed across valley districts. The Manipur government responded by ordering all schools and colleges closed for three days from August 20, 2026. No fresh injuries, arrests or clashes were reported in the current intelligence.", "Medical access: No specific information on hospitals, ambulances on site, or medical access issues was available in the search results. No injuries have been reported in the current phase of the protest.", "Legal support: No information on legal organisations, lawyers, helplines or the legal status of any detained protesters was available in the search results. No court interventions were mentioned."],
