    "name": "MPSC Job Aspirants Protest for Recruitment Reforms in Aizawl",
    "location": "Mizoram Public Service Commission (MPSC) office, New Secretariat Complex, Aizawl",
    "cause": "Student job aspirants are protesting outside the Mizoram Public Service Commission (MPSC) office, demanding reforms to the state recruitment process. They allege irregularities, lack of transparency, and delays in examinations and result declarations that affect thousands of government job seekers in Mizoram.",
    "dangerLevel": "moderate",
    "dangerReason": "The protest has remained largely peaceful since it began on August 10, 2026, with only a brief scuffle reported and no confirmed injuries or mass detentions. Protesters have picketed the MPSC office and prevented staff from entering, representing a physical blockade of government premises, but there are no reports of lathi charges, water cannons, tear gas, or mass arrests. The government's decision to form a reform committee and engage in talks with MZP leaders signals a de-escalatory posture, reducing the immediate risk of violent confrontation, though tensions could rise if the committee's outcomes are seen as inadequate.",
    "status": "Hundreds of Mizo Zirlai Pawl (MZP) members and job aspirants have been picketing outside the Mizoram Public Service Commission (MPSC) office at the New Secretariat Complex in Aizawl since Monday, August 10, 2026, demanding recruitment reforms over alleged irregularities and OTR exclusions. The MPSC has indefinitely postponed personal interviews for four posts and examinations scheduled from August 11 to 14, 2026, until further notice. Following talks with MZP leaders, affected students, and officials, the Mizoram government has decided to constitute an MPSC reform committee to strengthen the commission and improve its recruitment process. The MPSC stated it is 'not trying to create difficulties for job applicants, but is trying to make the recruitment process fair, transparent.' The MZP has indicated it will continue the agitation until concrete reforms are announced.",
    "details": ["Police presence: No specific police deployment numbers or equipment reported; protesters have picketed the MPSC office and prevented staff from entering, indicating a physical blockade of government premises.", "Recent incidents: A brief scuffle was reported during the picketing, but no injuries or mass detentions have been confirmed; the MPSC postponed interviews and exams scheduled for August 11-14, 2026.", "Medical access: No injuries or medical access issues have been reported; hospitals nearby are accessible, but no ambulances or medical personnel are mentioned as being on site.", "Legal support: No legal organizations or lawyers are mentioned as involved; no detentions or court interventions have been reported, and the government has engaged in talks with MZP leaders."],
