    "dangerLevel": "moderate",
    "dangerReason": "The protest has been largely peaceful, with no reported injuries or mass detentions, but a brief scuffle between police and protesters occurred when officials tried to enter the MPSC office, indicating a potential for escalation. The government's concessions—postponing exams and forming a reform panel—have somewhat eased tensions, but the ongoing nature of the agitation and involvement of students and youth keep the risk at a moderate level. Police presence remains visible but restrained, and there is no evidence of widespread violence or arrests.",
    "status": "Students, youth, and members of the public in Aizawl have been protesting since July 22, 2025, demanding reforms in the state's recruitment processes, including transparency in MPSC hiring. Protesters picketed the MPSC office, preventing officers and staff from entering, and rallied in central Aizawl, slowing traffic until evening. A brief scuffle occurred between police and some protesters when officials attempted to enter the MPSC office, but the protest remained largely peaceful. In response, the Mizoram Public Service Commission indefinitely postponed several recruitment exams and interviews, and the state government announced a panel to reform the MPSC. Organizers have indicated they will continue until concrete reforms are implemented.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Visible but restrained at MPSC office and central Aizawl; no reports of barricades, water cannons, or mass deployment.", "Recent incidents: Brief scuffle between police and protesters when officials attempted to enter MPSC office; no injuries or arrests reported.", "Medical access: No reports of injuries or medical access issues; hospitals in Aizawl remain accessible.", "Legal support: No reports of arrests or legal proceedings; student bodies like MZP involved in negotiations."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-06T00:18:59+00:00","level":"moderate","status":"On July 22, Aizawl witnessed a significant protest involving students, youth, and members of the public demanding reforms in the state's recruitment system. Participants gathered in central Aizawl and"},{"date":"2026-10-10T12:11:31+00:00","level":"moderate","status":"On July 22, students, youth, and members of the public gathered in central Aizawl and marched through main thoroughfares to demand reforms in the state's recruitment processes, with a focus on transpa"},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:11:49+00:00","level":"moderate","status":"Students, youth, and members of the public in Aizawl have been protesting since July 22, 2025, demanding reforms in the state's recruitment processes, including transparency in MPSC hiring. Protesters"},{"date":"2026-10-13T00:12:21+00:00","level":"moderate","status":"Students, youth, and members of the public in Aizawl have been protesting since July 22, 2025, demanding reforms in the state's recruitment processes, including transparency in MPSC hiring. Protesters"}]
