    "location": "Aizawl city centre, marching from Treasury Square to Raj Bhavan via Millennium Centre",
    "cause": "Protesting the proposed Foreign Contribution (Regulation) Amendment Bill 2026, which church leaders warn will enable government seizure of church and NGO assets and cripple foreign-funded charitable, educational, and missionary work across Mizoram.",
    "dangerLevel": "moderate",
    "dangerReason": "The August 11, 2026 rally in Aizawl drew thousands of participants but remained peaceful, with no reported injuries, arrests, or clashes between protesters and police. Police maintained a visible but non-confrontational presence, and organisers coordinated with the district administration to keep the march orderly. The primary risks are crowd density and traffic disruption on Aizawl's narrow hill roads rather than any violent confrontation, though the large scale of mobilisation and ongoing agitation warrant continued monitoring.",
    "status": "Thousands of people from various Christian denominations participated in a mass rally in Aizawl on Tuesday, August 11, 2026, organised by the Council of Churches in Mizoram (CCM) to protest the proposed FCRA Amendment Bill 2026. Participants gathered at Treasury Square and marched through the city centre toward Raj Bhavan, carrying placards and banners warning that the bill would enable government seizure of church and NGO assets and cripple foreign-funded charitable work. The rally remained peaceful, with no reports of clashes or arrests. Chief Minister Lalduhoma and church leaders are planning a delegation to meet Union Home Minister Amit Shah, while the Centre has indicated it may refer the bill to a Joint Parliamentary Committee amid widespread backlash. Organisers have vowed sustained agitation until the bill is withdrawn.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Visible but non-confrontational in Aizawl city centre; no reports of barricades, water cannons, or road closures; organisers coordinated with district administration.", "Recent incidents: Peaceful mass rally on August 11, 2026 from Treasury Square to Raj Bhavan; no injuries, arrests, or property damage reported; Baptist Church held mass prayer.", "Medical access: No injuries reported; hospitals in Aizawl available but not specifically mentioned in connection with the rally; no ambulances on site noted.", "Legal support: No arrests or detentions reported; CM Lalduhoma and church leaders planning delegation to meet Amit Shah; Centre may refer bill to JPC."],
