    "status": "Hundreds of students from schools and educational institutions across Mizoram staged a protest in Aizawl on Wednesday, July 22, 2026, over alleged NEET paper leaks, demanding the resignation of the Education Minister. The students gathered in the city center, carrying placards and banners, and traffic slowed across central Aizawl as the rally continued until evening. On July 24, Chief Minister Lalduhoma expressed solidarity with the students' peaceful movement, and the BJP's Mizoram unit also backed calls for a fair probe. No arrests or injuries have been reported, and the protest remained peaceful with police maintaining a visible but non-intervening presence. Student leaders have indicated they will continue demonstrations until their demands are addressed.",
