    "name": "Anti-Siang Dam Protest & Crackdown Resistance",
    "location": "Siang Valley (affected villages), with protest actions and solidarity gatherings reported in Itanagar and near the Arunachal Pradesh Civil Secretariat",
    "cause": "Villagers and activists are opposing the proposed Siang Dam project, demanding meaningful consultation and participation in official meetings. They are also protesting the escalating government crackdown on anti-dam activists, including a CBI case under FCRA, police summons, and restrictions on local news pages covering the movement.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level is critical due to the government's invocation of the Arunachal Pradesh Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act (APUAPA) and the detention of at least four individuals from Geku, Upper Siang district, as of October 9. This follows the arrest of at least five people in the Siang valley on October 5, indicating a rapid escalation in the crackdown. The protests have turned violent, with reports of clashes between villagers and security forces, though specific details of injuries are not provided. The use of UAPA, a stringent anti-terror law, against protesters signals a severe government posture and raises the risk of prolonged detention without bail. The situation is further aggravated by restrictions on local news pages covering the movement, limiting information flow and increasing the potential for unchecked escalation.",
    "status": "The anti-Siang Upper Multipurpose Project (SUMP) protest movement in Arunachal Pradesh remains active and tense as of the latest reports. On October 5, at least five people were arrested in the Siang valley as the government intensified its crackdown on dissent, according to Tongam Rina. Four residents from Geku in Upper Siang district, previously reported missing, were detained under the Arunachal Pradesh Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act (APUAPA) on October 9, as reported by The Arunachal Times. On Saturday, anti-dam groups staged a rally at Dite Dime in Siang district against NHPC's proposed 12,500MW project. In Geku, hundreds of Adi villagers protested demanding the release of six detainees and issued an ultimatum to the district administration over the controversial mega-dam survey. The situation remains tense with a high risk of further detentions and clashes, and organizers are continuing to mobilize affected communities.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Specific numbers and equipment not detailed in available reports. Security forces have been deployed in Siang valley and Upper Siang district to enforce detentions and manage protests. Road closures or barricades not explicitly mentioned.", "Recent incidents: On October 5, at least five people were arrested in Siang valley. On October 9, four residents from Geku were detained under APUAPA after being reported missing. On Saturday, a rally was held at Dite Dime in Siang district. In Geku, hundreds protested demanding release of six detainees and issued an ultimatum.", "Medical access: No information available on hospitals, ambulances, or injuries. Reports do not mention medical access issues or injuries requiring treatment.", "Legal support: Detainees held under APUAPA, which allows prolonged detention without bail. No specific legal aid organizations or helplines mentioned. Court interventions not reported. Local news pages restricted, limiting information dissemination."],
