    "dangerReason": "The danger level is assessed as high due to the government's invocation of the stringent APUAPA and the detention of four protesters from Geku on 9 October, indicating a serious escalation in legal and police response. Prohibitory orders under Section 163 were imposed ahead of a massive rally at Yingkiong, and thousands participated despite the restrictions, raising the risk of confrontations. Notices served to government employees and village heads further demonstrate a punitive posture, and the demand for release of those arrested in connection with recent violent incidents indicates that clashes have already occurred, though specific details of injuries or property damage are not available in the search results.",
    "status": "The anti-SUMP protest movement in Arunachal Pradesh remains active and has intensified, with thousands participating in a rally at Yingkiong in the Siang region demanding the release of those arrested in connection with recent violent incidents. The district administration had imposed prohibitory orders under Section 163 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita ahead of the rally. On 9 October, the government invoked the Arunachal Pradesh Unlawful Activities (Prevention) Act (APUAPA) and detained four residents from Geku in Upper Siang district who were previously reported missing. Earlier, on 14 September, villagers from Komkar and surrounding areas staged protests at two proposed SUMP dam sites against PFR activities. Notices have also been served on several government employees and gaon burahs for their participation in protests. No next steps have been formally announced by organisers.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Prohibitory orders under Section 163 imposed in Yingkiong; exact police numbers and equipment not specified in reports.", "Recent incidents: Four residents detained under APUAPA on 9 Oct; thousands rallied at Yingkiong demanding release of those arrested in recent violent incidents.", "Medical access: No information available in search results regarding hospitals, ambulances, or injuries.", "Legal support: APUAPA invoked; notices served on government employees and gaon burahs; no legal aid organizations or helplines mentioned."],
