    "status": "An indefinite bandh began in Arunachal Pradesh's Namsai district on Friday morning, with protesters blocking key roads and forcing commercial establishments to shut down across the Lekang constituency. The strike was called in response to new uniform eligibility criteria for government recruitment that demonstrators argue discriminate against local job seekers. Bandh supporters have been patrolling major intersections and market areas to enforce the shutdown, while district administration officials have not yet announced any formal negotiations with protest leaders. Police have been deployed to sensitive locations to prevent untoward incidents, but no arrests or injuries have been confirmed so far. Protest organisers have stated the bandh will continue indefinitely until the state government revises the recruitment rules, and they have threatened to extend the agitation to other districts if their demands are not met.",
