    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains high because TMPK has stepped up its economic blockade at multiple border points, directly disrupting supply routes into Itanagar and affecting daily life. The blockade follows the August 10 firing at Hime in which a Mising youth was killed and at least 11–12 people were injured, and TMPK has warned against mistaking Assamese restraint for weakness, indicating a potential for escalation. While no new mass violence has been reported in the current search results, the ongoing blockade and heightened rhetoric create a tense standoff with risk of confrontation.",
