    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains moderate because the protest has de-escalated: the indefinite hunger strike was put on hold on February 13, and the core committee decided to temporarily pause the protest while setting a June 2026 cut-off. The earlier scuffle with police and one injury during an attempt to storm the Secretariat remains a concern, but no recent violence or mass detentions have been reported. The government has engaged through the School Education Department, stating the regularisation process is underway, which reduces immediate tension. However, the underlying grievance persists, and the June 2026 deadline could lead to renewed escalation if unmet.",
    "status": "The ANATG 2015 batch ad hoc teachers' protest at the Nagaland Civil Secretariat in Kohima has been temporarily paused by the core committee, with a June 2026 cut-off set for the government to resolve the regularisation of 1,166 teachers. Over 1,000 teachers had participated in sit-in demonstrations, which briefly turned violent on a Friday when frustrated demonstrators attempted to storm the Secretariat, leading to a scuffle with police and at least one injury. The protest entered its third and fourth days with intensified sit-ins, but on February 13, the group put its indefinite hunger strike on hold and vowed to continue peaceful sit-ins. The School Education Department stated that the regularisation process is underway but no fixed date has been provided. The core committee decided to temporarily pause the protest, but the underlying grievance persists.",
