    "status": "Puducherry DMK legislators and cadre staged a road roko on East Coast Road (ECR) near the Puducherry–Tamil Nadu border checkpoint on Tuesday, August 4, 2026, protesting the arrest of Tamil Nadu Leader of the Opposition Udhayanidhi Stalin. Puducherry police detained four DMK MLAs and several cadres, removing them from the scene to clear the road. DMK workers, led by R. Siva, also staged a protest in Puducherry courting arrest over Udhayanidhi Stalin's detention in Chennai. Similar protests occurred across Tamil Nadu, including in Tiruchi, Salem, Namakkal, and Tirunelveli, where over 300 arrests were made in Salem and Namakkal and a youth was assaulted in Tirunelveli. DMK has indicated it will continue agitational programmes if Udhayanidhi Stalin is not released promptly, with further protests planned across the Union Territory.",
