    "status": "Sonam Wangchuk led a candle march in Leh on Monday from the Main Market to Polo Ground, with around 500 participants carrying candles and placards to honour those killed in the September 24, 2025 Ladakh violence. The march was peaceful with no confrontations reported, and Wangchuk, released in March 2026 after six months in jail, addressed the crowd at Polo Ground, demanding the release of the Inquiry Commission's report and accountability for alleged police brutality, stating that people were shot in the head during the crackdown. He also criticised the Lieutenant Governor's compensation for victims as inadequate. The district administration has not issued any statement regarding the report's release, and protestors have announced a relay hunger strike at Polo Ground starting tomorrow if the report is not made public within 72 hours.",
