    "status": "US Ambassador Sergio Gor visited Leh in July 2026, and his remark calling Jammu and Kashmir an 'important part of India' triggered protests in Leh and a formal diplomatic row with Pakistan. In Leh, demonstrators gathered in Main Bazaar carrying placards opposing foreign interference in Kashmir's status, with some groups also criticizing the US position on Iran. The crowd size remained in the low hundreds, and police maintained a visible but non-confrontational presence along the envoy's route. Pakistan summoned the US envoy in Islamabad to protest the remarks, while Indian officials welcomed the statement. Organizers say further rallies will be held if the US makes additional comments on Kashmir, and a solidarity march is being planned near the Leh DC office.",
