    "name": "Qaumi Insaaf Morcha Protest at Mohali-Chandigarh Border",
    "location": "Mohali-Chandigarh border (Sector 43/Phase 8 area), near the barricaded entry points to Chandigarh",
    "cause": "The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha is demanding justice for Sikh prisoners, including the release of those who have completed their sentences, and has escalated to a Punjab Bandh call for August 21. The morcha is also seeking parole for prisoners convicted in the former Punjab CM Beant Singh assassination case.",
    "dangerLevel": "critical",
    "dangerReason": "The danger level remains critical due to confirmed police violence on August 15, 2026, when water cannons and tear gas were deployed against protesters attempting to breach barricades at the Mohali-Chandigarh border. Multiple injuries were reported amid chaotic clashes, and the confrontation escalated as protesters marched toward the Punjab Raj Bhavan. The situation is further aggravated by the Punjab Bandh call for August 21, 2026, which has led to heightened security and potential for widespread disruption. The involvement of the SGPC and the emotive nature of the demands (release of Sikh prisoners) increase the risk of mass mobilization and further confrontations. Police have fortified the border with anti-riot vehicles and barbed wire, indicating a readiness for continued force, while protesters remain defiant.",
    "status": "The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border remains active and tense, with hundreds of activists continuing their sit-in and attempting marches toward the Punjab Governor's residence and Punjab Lok Bhawan. On Saturday, August 15, 2026, police used water cannons and tear gas to stop protesters who tried to forcibly breach barricades at the border, resulting in chaotic scenes and injuries. The morcha has called for a Punjab Bandh on August 21, 2026, which saw a mixed response across the state, with tight security at the Chandigarh-Mohali border and disruptions to normal life. The protest has received backing from the Shiromani Gurdwara Parbandhak Committee (SGPC), adding to its strength. Protesters are demanding the release of Sikh prisoners (Bandi Singhs) who have completed their sentences, including parole for those convicted in the Beant Singh assassination case. Police have fortified the border with additional barricades, barbed wire, and anti-riot vehicles, and both sides remain entrenched with no resolution in sight.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Heavy police deployment at the Chandigarh-Mohali border, with barricades, barbed wire, and anti-riot vehicles. Water cannons and tear gas used on August 15, 2026. Tight security also reported for the August 21 bandh.", "Recent incidents: On August 15, 2026, protesters attempted to breach barricades and march toward the Governor's residence; police responded with water cannons and tear gas, causing injuries and chaotic scenes. A Punjab Bandh on August 21, 2026, saw mixed response with disruptions.", "Medical access: No specific information available on medical access or hospitals in the search results.", "Legal support: No specific information available on legal support or organizations involved in the search results."],
    "trendHistory": [{"date":"2026-10-10T04:12:03+00:00","level":"critical","status":"The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest has intensified significantly, with hundreds of protesters gathering at the Mohali-Chandigarh border since mid-August 2026. On August 15, police used tear gas and water"},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:02:36+00:00","level":"critical","status":"The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest has intensified significantly, with hundreds of protesters gathering at the Mohali-Chandigarh border since mid-August 2026. On August 15, police used tear gas and water"},{"date":"2026-10-12T00:03:30+00:00","level":"critical","status":"The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border remains active and tense, with hundreds of activists continuing their sit-in and attempting marches toward the Punjab Governor's residen"},{"date":"2026-10-14T00:09:37+00:00","level":"critical","status":"The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border remains active and tense, with hundreds of activists continuing their sit-in and attempting marches toward the Punjab Governor's residen"},{"date":"2026-10-16T00:10:55+00:00","level":"critical","status":"The Qaumi Insaaf Morcha protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border remains active and tense, with hundreds of activists continuing their sit-in and attempting marches toward the Punjab Governor's residen"}]
