    "status": "The Bandi Sikh March in Chandigarh, backed by the Shiromani Gurdwara Parbandhak Committee (SGPC) and Qaumi Insaaf Morcha, remains an active and volatile protest as of late August 2026. On August 21, 2026, the Qaumi Insaaf Morcha called a Punjab bandh, which crippled transport and shut markets across the state. During the bandh, protesters attempting to march towards Chandigarh clashed with police at the Chandigarh-Mohali border after trying to breach barricades; police responded with water cannons and tear gas. The march to Punjab Raj Bhavan was denied permission, and a large police deployment, including RAF and paramilitary units, was in place. A jailed extremist's video surfaced on August 20, 2026, calling for mass mobilization, adding to tensions. Protesters have vowed to continue their agitation, with SGPC announcing a parallel peaceful sit-in if blocked.",
