    "name": "Chandigarh Traffic Diversions Ahead of SKM Farmer Protest",
    "location": "Mohali-Chandigarh border (Phase 8/ Sector 48-49 area), with diversions across Chandigarh",
    "cause": "Samyukta Kisan Morcha (SKM) is holding a week-long farmer protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border from September 1-7, demanding resolution of pending agricultural issues including MSP guarantees and debt relief. The protest is part of a broader SKM call for farmer rights.",
    "dangerLevel": "moderate",
    "dangerReason": "The protest is large-scale, with 2,000 tractors and 10,000+ farmers expected, and has triggered significant traffic diversions across Chandigarh from August 31. However, search results do not report any police violence, detentions, injuries, or clashes; the police posture appears focused on traffic management and barricading rather than active enforcement of Section 144. The main risks are traffic chaos, road closures, and potential escalation if barricades are breached, but current evidence does not justify a higher danger level.",
    "status": "The Samyukta Kisan Morcha (SKM) is holding a week-long farmer protest at the Mohali-Chandigarh border from September 1-7, with around 2,000 tractors and over 200 tractor-trailers having reached the Faidan barrier. Chandigarh traffic police enforced diversions and restrictions from August 31, affecting Airport Road, Jan Marg, Sector 43 and key junctions. The protest is part of a broader SKM call over agricultural demands including MSP guarantees and debt relief, and is linked to opposition to the India-US trade deal. No reports of violence or clashes have emerged so far, and the situation remains a traffic and crowd-management challenge rather than an active confrontation.",
    "details": ["Police presence: Chandigarh traffic police enforced diversions from August 31 on Airport Road, Jan Marg, Sector 43 and key junctions; no specific numbers or equipment reported.", "Recent incidents: No violence, detentions, or injuries reported; 200 tractor-trailers reached Faidan barrier and 2,000 tractors are expected at the Mohali-Chandigarh border.", "Medical access: No reports of injuries or medical access issues; hospitals in Chandigarh and Mohali are accessible but traffic diversions may delay emergency vehicles.", "Legal support: No legal interventions or detentions reported; SKM organisers are coordinating with authorities on traffic management."],
