    "location": "Island-wide bandh affecting Port Blair, including Aberdeen Bazaar, Mohanpura, and Haddo areas",
    "cause": "Student groups have called for a complete Andaman bandh to strengthen their ongoing protest against the proposed shift of Andaman College (ANCOL) to a new university campus. Students argue the move will disrupt access to education, displace existing facilities, and ignore the concerns of the local student community.",
    "dangerLevel": "moderate",
    "dangerReason": "The protest has shifted toward legal and symbolic action, with organisers announcing on 22 February 2026 that they will file a court case and hold a candle march rather than escalating to confrontational tactics. The earlier island-wide bandh on 16 February 2026 carried inherent risks of forced closures and road blockades, but no verified reports of violence, injuries, arrests or lathi charges have surfaced in the available search intelligence. With the movement now channelled into judicial and peaceful forms of protest, the danger level is assessed as moderate rather than high.",
    "status": "The Joint Action Forum's agitation against the proposed shift of Andaman College (ANCOL) and six other colleges from Pondicherry University affiliation to a deemed university remains active, with the most recent reported activity dated 22 February 2026 at JNRM in Port Blair. According to the available report, the Joint Action Forum announced it will file a case in court on Monday morning challenging the proposed shift and is also planning a candle march. The earlier full-day Andaman Bandh called for 16 February 2026 (6 am to 8 pm) across the islands, with concentration in Aberdeen Bazaar, Mohanpura and Haddo, formed part of this same ongoing agitation that began on 3 February 2026. No verified reports of violence, injuries, arrests or lathi charges have emerged in the available intelligence, and the administration has continued to defend the shift as necessary for infrastructure upgrades while students demand a reversal and a central university.",
    "details": ["Police presence: No specific police deployment numbers, equipment, or road closures were mentioned in the available search intelligence for the 22 February 2026 JNRM activity or the 16 February 2026 bandh.", "Recent incidents: On 22 February 2026, the Joint Action Forum announced at JNRM, Port Blair, that it will file a court case on Monday morning and plans a candle march; no injuries, arrests, or property damage were reported.", "Medical access: No hospitals, ambulances, or injury details were referenced in the available search results; no medical access concerns have been reported.", "Legal support: The Joint Action Forum itself is pursuing legal action, announcing on 22 February 2026 that it will file a case in court on Monday morning against the proposed shift; no other organizations, helplines, or court interventions were mentioned."],
